1
00:00:04,733 --> 00:00:07,600
♪ In the not-to-distant future ♪

2
00:00:07,600 --> 00:00:11,067
♪ Next Sunday A.D. ♪

3
00:00:11,067 --> 00:00:13,867
♪ There was a guy named Joel ♪

4
00:00:13,867 --> 00:00:17,367
♪ Not too different
from you or me ♪

5
00:00:17,367 --> 00:00:20,133
♪ He worked at
Gizmonic Institute ♪

6
00:00:20,133 --> 00:00:23,667
♪ Just another face
in a red jumpsuit ♪

7
00:00:23,667 --> 00:00:26,433
♪ He did a good job
cleaning up the place ♪

8
00:00:26,433 --> 00:00:27,967
♪ But his bosses
didn't like him ♪

9
00:00:27,967 --> 00:00:32,833
♪ So they shot him into space ♪

10
00:00:32,833 --> 00:00:36,067
♪ We'll send him cheesy movies ♪

11
00:00:36,067 --> 00:00:38,167
♪ The worst we can find ♪

12
00:00:38,167 --> 00:00:39,500
♪ La la la ♪

13
00:00:39,500 --> 00:00:42,000
♪ He'll have to sit
and watch them all ♪

14
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:44,433
♪ Then we'll monitor his mind ♪

15
00:00:44,433 --> 00:00:45,767
♪ La la la ♪

16
00:00:45,767 --> 00:00:48,267
♪ Now keep in mind
Joel can't control ♪

17
00:00:48,267 --> 00:00:50,833
♪ Where the movies
begin or end ♪

18
00:00:50,833 --> 00:00:52,067
♪ La la la ♪

19
00:00:52,067 --> 00:00:54,567
♪ Because he used
those special parts ♪

20
00:00:54,567 --> 00:00:59,400
♪ To make his robot friends ♪

21
00:00:59,400 --> 00:01:00,967
♪ Robot Roll Call ♪

22
00:01:00,967 --> 00:01:02,533
♪ Cambot ♪

23
00:01:02,533 --> 00:01:03,767
♪ Gypsy ♪

24
00:01:03,767 --> 00:01:05,667
♪ Tom Servo ♪

25
00:01:05,667 --> 00:01:07,067
♪ Croooow! ♪

26
00:01:07,067 --> 00:01:10,200
♪ You're wondering how
he eats and breathes ♪

27
00:01:10,200 --> 00:01:12,433
♪ And other science facts ♪

28
00:01:12,433 --> 00:01:13,867
♪ La la la ♪

29
00:01:13,867 --> 00:01:16,233
♪ Then repeat to yourself
it's just a show ♪

30
00:01:16,233 --> 00:01:19,167
♪ I should really just relax ♪

31
00:01:19,167 --> 00:01:23,400
♪ For Mystery Science
Theater 3000 ♪

32
00:01:35,067 --> 00:01:37,000
- I know, I know.

33
00:01:37,000 --> 00:01:39,300
Hi, everybody. Welcome
to the Satellite of Love.

34
00:01:39,300 --> 00:01:42,233
Gypsy's feeling king of
depressed today, you know.

35
00:01:42,233 --> 00:01:43,767
A lot of people
don't realize this

36
00:01:43,767 --> 00:01:46,667
but she has a lot of
responsibilities on the ship.

37
00:01:46,667 --> 00:01:48,200
- Yeah, like we don't have any.

38
00:01:48,200 --> 00:01:49,967
- Hey now, listen,
you guys, you know,

39
00:01:49,967 --> 00:01:51,967
she's the one who keeps a
lot of the higher system

40
00:01:51,967 --> 00:01:53,400
functions running on the ship

41
00:01:53,400 --> 00:01:55,600
so you guys can gallivant
around, all right?

42
00:01:55,600 --> 00:01:57,933
That's why sometimes she's
kinda hard to understand.

43
00:01:57,933 --> 00:02:00,333
- Yeah, that's why she
sounds like Moms Mabley.

44
00:02:00,333 --> 00:02:01,200
(Crow and Servo laugh)

45
00:02:01,200 --> 00:02:02,000
- That's great.

46
00:02:02,000 --> 00:02:02,933
Now listen, you guys.

47
00:02:02,933 --> 00:02:04,400
I'm gonna have to ask Gypsy

48
00:02:04,400 --> 00:02:06,833
to shut down some of the higher
functions she's been slaving

49
00:02:06,833 --> 00:02:10,000
so she can free up her mind
and tell me what's bugging her.

50
00:02:10,000 --> 00:02:10,833
Now I need...

51
00:02:10,833 --> 00:02:12,333
Now I need you to...

52
00:02:12,333 --> 00:02:14,067
Now would you guys look at
me when I'm talking to you?

53
00:02:14,067 --> 00:02:15,600
All right, now I'm
gonna need you guys

54
00:02:15,600 --> 00:02:18,167
to finally do some work around
here for a change, capisce?

55
00:02:18,167 --> 00:02:20,667
- [Computer] Commercial
sign in 15 seconds.

56
00:02:20,667 --> 00:02:21,900
- Now Tom Servo,

57
00:02:21,900 --> 00:02:23,367
I want you to go down
to the Maneuvering Room

58
00:02:23,367 --> 00:02:25,100
and keep those heat shields
pointed towards the sun.

59
00:02:25,100 --> 00:02:26,000
Crow,

60
00:02:26,000 --> 00:02:28,067
I need you to do

61
00:02:28,067 --> 00:02:29,200
everything else, all right?

62
00:02:29,200 --> 00:02:30,833
And stay frosty, you two.

63
00:02:30,833 --> 00:02:31,933
- Cool.
- Check.

64
00:02:31,933 --> 00:02:33,667
- [Computer] Commercial
sign in five,

65
00:02:33,667 --> 00:02:35,800
four, three, two...

66
00:02:35,800 --> 00:02:36,867
Commercial sign now.

67
00:02:36,867 --> 00:02:38,700
- We'll be right back.

68
00:02:44,867 --> 00:02:48,033
- And so, I guess I'm just
feeling the old ennui, you know.

69
00:02:48,033 --> 00:02:50,233
It's nothing, I'm just
a little depressed.

70
00:02:50,233 --> 00:02:51,633
Look, you're busy.

71
00:02:51,633 --> 00:02:53,367
We'll talk about this later.

72
00:02:53,367 --> 00:02:54,700
I'll re-initiate the astronic

73
00:02:54,700 --> 00:02:56,800
and photonic systems on my mark.

74
00:02:56,800 --> 00:02:57,600
Re-initiate!

75
00:02:58,500 --> 00:03:01,200
(Joel coughs)

76
00:03:01,200 --> 00:03:02,833
- Thanks, Gypsy.

77
00:03:02,833 --> 00:03:04,867
I'm real glad we could
have this little talk.

78
00:03:04,867 --> 00:03:06,500
- Richard Basehart!

79
00:03:06,500 --> 00:03:08,100
- Right, Richard
Basehart, that's right.

80
00:03:08,100 --> 00:03:09,400
- Howdy, Cap'n!

81
00:03:09,400 --> 00:03:10,867
- Hey, stud!

82
00:03:10,867 --> 00:03:13,700
- You know, I had the
nicest talk with Gypsy.

83
00:03:13,700 --> 00:03:16,200
She's a really warm
and wonderful person.

84
00:03:16,200 --> 00:03:19,267
- Uh, Joel, the
scientists are calling.

85
00:03:19,267 --> 00:03:22,333
- Yeah, I just feel like
she's my new best friend.

86
00:03:22,333 --> 00:03:23,800
I can't even describe it.

87
00:03:23,800 --> 00:03:26,133
- Well don't try 'cause
the scientists are calling.

88
00:03:26,133 --> 00:03:26,967
- Oh, okay.

89
00:03:28,100 --> 00:03:30,600
- No, Joel, the
button's over there.

90
00:03:30,600 --> 00:03:32,200
- I'll get it.

91
00:03:32,200 --> 00:03:33,367
- [Servo] For crying out loud.

92
00:03:33,367 --> 00:03:35,867
- Oh, hello, Joel-erini Weenie!

93
00:03:35,867 --> 00:03:36,800
Is that funny, Frank?

94
00:03:36,800 --> 00:03:38,067
Have we used that one before?

95
00:03:38,067 --> 00:03:39,700
- Uh, no.

96
00:03:39,700 --> 00:03:42,100
- Well, Joel, it's time
for the invention exchange.

97
00:03:42,100 --> 00:03:43,967
You may wonder why
we're dressed this way.

98
00:03:43,967 --> 00:03:45,500
- I wonder.
- Shut up.

99
00:03:45,500 --> 00:03:47,467
We're dressed this way because
I've lost my train of thought

100
00:03:47,467 --> 00:03:50,367
and don't you ever interrupt
me when I'm on a roll again!

101
00:03:51,767 --> 00:03:53,833
- [Both] We're dressed
this way because of the...

102
00:03:55,133 --> 00:03:56,733
- Anyway, Joel, as you know,

103
00:03:56,733 --> 00:03:59,667
children have long looked up
to cowboys as role models.

104
00:03:59,667 --> 00:04:00,967
And vice-versa.

105
00:04:00,967 --> 00:04:03,200
That's where we get
the hobby horse from.

106
00:04:03,200 --> 00:04:04,433
But today kids are looking

107
00:04:04,433 --> 00:04:06,733
for more sophisticated
role models.

108
00:04:06,733 --> 00:04:08,000
What's that thing, Frank?

109
00:04:09,133 --> 00:04:12,000
- Kookoo kids lookin'
for kookoo kicks.

110
00:04:12,000 --> 00:04:14,400
(clucks goofily)

111
00:04:14,400 --> 00:04:15,433
- Yeah, anyway.

112
00:04:16,600 --> 00:04:18,100
- So what we've done,

113
00:04:18,100 --> 00:04:20,367
and since today's movie
is kind of a biker movie,

114
00:04:20,367 --> 00:04:22,200
what we've done is we've taken

115
00:04:22,200 --> 00:04:23,967
the whole hobby horse concept,

116
00:04:23,967 --> 00:04:26,167
we've pared it down a bit,
shot some paint on it.

117
00:04:26,167 --> 00:04:28,367
And what we have here is the...

118
00:04:28,367 --> 00:04:29,400
the Hobby Hog!

119
00:04:29,400 --> 00:04:31,300
Woo!
(engines revving)

120
00:04:31,300 --> 00:04:32,833
- That's right!

121
00:04:32,833 --> 00:04:35,167
It's for kids who want to
get into concert security!

122
00:04:35,167 --> 00:04:37,167
But we haven't forgot the child!

123
00:04:37,167 --> 00:04:39,000
The saddlebags are
filled with zwieback

124
00:04:39,000 --> 00:04:41,300
and the tank's
filled with Bosco!

125
00:04:41,300 --> 00:04:42,667
Kick it down, mamma jamma!

126
00:04:43,700 --> 00:04:45,367
(engines rev)

127
00:04:45,367 --> 00:04:47,333
- Hey, I'm sorry,
I wasn't listening.

128
00:04:47,333 --> 00:04:50,033
Cambot, could you bring
it out a little bit?

129
00:04:50,033 --> 00:04:53,200
All right, there's nothing
the fellas and me enjoy more

130
00:04:53,200 --> 00:04:55,167
than a big, juicy, sloppy pizza

131
00:04:55,167 --> 00:04:57,000
before we head on
in for an experiment

132
00:04:57,000 --> 00:04:59,167
in the Mystery Science Theater.

133
00:04:59,167 --> 00:05:01,400
Anyway, this is a
thing I invented.

134
00:05:01,400 --> 00:05:04,200
It kinda puts a high-tech
spin on an old standard.

135
00:05:04,200 --> 00:05:05,933
It's the 3D pizza.

136
00:05:05,933 --> 00:05:08,300
I based it on the
premise of the 3D chess

137
00:05:08,300 --> 00:05:09,967
from the old Star Trek show.

138
00:05:09,967 --> 00:05:12,200
- It's even better
with the 3D glasses on.

139
00:05:12,200 --> 00:05:13,633
I feel like I'm really here!

140
00:05:13,633 --> 00:05:14,767
- Let's see, uh...

141
00:05:14,767 --> 00:05:17,467
Pepperoni to
anchovy, level four.

142
00:05:17,467 --> 00:05:18,400
Check!

143
00:05:18,400 --> 00:05:19,467
I've got you now, Mr. Bond!

144
00:05:19,467 --> 00:05:21,267
- And if you've got extra,

145
00:05:21,267 --> 00:05:24,233
you can take and use this neat
pizza lunch box I invented

146
00:05:24,233 --> 00:05:26,500
and carry it right into the
Mystery Science Theater.

147
00:05:26,500 --> 00:05:28,700
- Joel, that's a trash can lid.

148
00:05:29,900 --> 00:05:31,167
- Oh.

149
00:05:31,167 --> 00:05:32,833
Well, you can use
it for that, too.

150
00:05:32,833 --> 00:05:34,200
What do you think, sirs?

151
00:05:34,200 --> 00:05:36,433
- I'm sorry, Joel,
we couldn't hear you!

152
00:05:38,333 --> 00:05:41,433
Your experiment today
is called Wild Rebels.

153
00:05:41,433 --> 00:05:44,167
- It's a cool,
swingin', heavy trip.

154
00:05:44,167 --> 00:05:45,800
(clucks goofily)

155
00:05:45,800 --> 00:05:47,300
- What is that noise?

156
00:05:47,300 --> 00:05:48,933
- It's just a sound, that's all.

157
00:05:48,933 --> 00:05:50,200
- I know, but you
do it all the time.

158
00:05:50,200 --> 00:05:52,100
- It's nothing really.
- What does it mean?

159
00:05:52,100 --> 00:05:54,067
It's about me, isn't it?
- No.

160
00:05:54,067 --> 00:05:55,000
(alarms buzzing)

161
00:05:55,000 --> 00:05:57,367
- [All] We've got movie sign!

162
00:06:07,300 --> 00:06:08,533
♪ Wild Rebels ♪

163
00:06:08,533 --> 00:06:10,033
♪ We're reckless ♪

164
00:06:10,033 --> 00:06:12,400
- [Servo] I wish I could eat
pizza, Joel, that looks good.

165
00:06:12,400 --> 00:06:13,833
- [Joel] Steve Lame-o.

166
00:06:16,533 --> 00:06:19,333
- [Crow] Hey, Pastrano!
My favorite sammich.

167
00:06:21,167 --> 00:06:23,233
- [Servo] And the
Glaucoma Players.

168
00:06:23,233 --> 00:06:25,700
Boy, I can hardly read
this, how about you?

169
00:06:28,900 --> 00:06:30,367
- [Joel] There's no way
we can read 'em all.

170
00:06:30,367 --> 00:06:33,300
And here's the people with
the really bad agents.

171
00:06:35,900 --> 00:06:37,200
- [Servo] That's impossible.

172
00:06:40,267 --> 00:06:41,467
- [Crow] Catchy tune.

173
00:06:41,467 --> 00:06:43,300
- [Servo] Okay, is
that better or worse?

174
00:06:43,300 --> 00:06:44,833
- [Joel] That's a little better.

175
00:06:46,867 --> 00:06:48,233
- [Servo] That's
gotta be better.

176
00:06:49,567 --> 00:06:50,467
How about this?

177
00:06:50,467 --> 00:06:51,467
- [Joel] That's worse.

178
00:06:51,467 --> 00:06:53,867
- [Servo] Better
one, better two?

179
00:06:53,867 --> 00:06:54,733
- [Joel] Better one.

180
00:06:54,733 --> 00:06:55,800
- [Servo] Okay, good.

181
00:06:57,000 --> 00:06:59,533
- [Crow] Comet Pictures,
a real flash in the pan.

182
00:07:01,233 --> 00:07:02,800
- [Joel] What's the extra E for?

183
00:07:02,800 --> 00:07:03,900
- [Crow] Well that's for extra--

184
00:07:03,900 --> 00:07:04,833
- [Servo] (coughing) Ixnay.

185
00:07:04,833 --> 00:07:06,067
- [Crow] I'll tell you later.

186
00:07:07,833 --> 00:07:10,233
(siren blaring)

187
00:07:10,233 --> 00:07:11,800
- [Servo] Trouble with the car?

188
00:07:14,200 --> 00:07:15,900
- [Joel] I'm here, Steve.

189
00:07:15,900 --> 00:07:17,500
- Tough break, Rod.

190
00:07:17,500 --> 00:07:19,233
- [Servo] That's Rod.

191
00:07:20,533 --> 00:07:21,800
- Man, it's not the work.

192
00:07:23,900 --> 00:07:26,733
- [Joel] I don't think
the scene's over yet, Rod.

193
00:07:28,067 --> 00:07:30,333
- There goes two
years of saving.

194
00:07:30,333 --> 00:07:31,767
- [Servo] Well you
shouldn't carry cash

195
00:07:31,767 --> 00:07:33,867
in the glove compartment, Rod.

196
00:07:33,867 --> 00:07:35,067
- Nothing.

197
00:07:35,067 --> 00:07:37,500
- Come on, Rod, you can
build another super.

198
00:07:37,500 --> 00:07:38,300
- What?

199
00:07:38,300 --> 00:07:39,700
Chewing gum and spit?

200
00:07:39,700 --> 00:07:40,967
- [Servo] No thanks, I just ate.

201
00:07:40,967 --> 00:07:42,600
- [Crow] By the way,
who are you anyway?

202
00:07:42,600 --> 00:07:44,100
- I wanna call it quits.

203
00:07:44,100 --> 00:07:45,800
- Hey, Rod, it's
all in the game!

204
00:07:45,800 --> 00:07:46,967
- [Crow] And who are you?

205
00:07:46,967 --> 00:07:47,967
- Some game.

206
00:07:51,967 --> 00:07:53,200
- [Joel] Paint your house.

207
00:07:53,200 --> 00:07:54,000
- [Servo] How's my
sandwich coming?

208
00:07:56,267 --> 00:07:57,633
- [Crow] Geez,
what a lousy day...

209
00:07:57,633 --> 00:07:58,567
What?

210
00:07:58,567 --> 00:08:00,367
What? What do you want from me?

211
00:08:00,367 --> 00:08:03,133
- [Servo] Down the
trail of shame he goes.

212
00:08:03,133 --> 00:08:04,033
- [Crow] Hippity hop.

213
00:08:05,900 --> 00:08:07,900
More like dragitty drag.

214
00:08:09,800 --> 00:08:10,633
Poor guy.

215
00:08:11,967 --> 00:08:13,200
Uh, oh.

216
00:08:13,200 --> 00:08:15,300
Here comes the sermon
on the Gran Turino.

217
00:08:16,233 --> 00:08:17,500
- Everybody!

218
00:08:17,500 --> 00:08:19,733
- [Joel] Blessed are
the grease monkeys,

219
00:08:19,733 --> 00:08:21,200
for they will lube...

220
00:08:21,200 --> 00:08:24,233
(Crow and Servo mimic grumbling)

221
00:08:24,233 --> 00:08:26,367
- [Servo] Wrap around here,
get in the shot, everybody.

222
00:08:26,367 --> 00:08:27,833
- [Joel] Gotta stay on camera.

223
00:08:29,300 --> 00:08:32,000
Hi, my name's Rod
and I'm a gasaholic.

224
00:08:32,000 --> 00:08:33,733
- [Crow And Servo] Hi, Rod!

225
00:08:33,733 --> 00:08:35,233
- This is an official auction.

226
00:08:36,133 --> 00:08:37,133
I got a new trailer over there.

227
00:08:37,133 --> 00:08:38,700
- [Joel] Hey, nice guitar.

228
00:08:38,700 --> 00:08:40,133
- Brand new tires and rims.

229
00:08:40,133 --> 00:08:41,167
What am I bid for it?

230
00:08:42,800 --> 00:08:43,700
- [Crow] Well I'll
take the guit--

231
00:08:43,700 --> 00:08:44,900
- [All] Huh?

232
00:08:44,900 --> 00:08:46,433
- Come on, don't be
bashful, what am I bid?

233
00:08:46,433 --> 00:08:47,433
They're brand new.

234
00:08:47,433 --> 00:08:48,500
- Come on down from there, Rod.

235
00:08:48,500 --> 00:08:49,700
You don't want to sell out.

236
00:08:49,700 --> 00:08:51,367
- [Servo] I made
this movie, didn't I?

237
00:08:51,367 --> 00:08:52,200
- I've had it.

238
00:08:53,633 --> 00:08:55,100
- [Servo] How about these
Robert Culp I Spy pants?

239
00:08:55,100 --> 00:08:57,300
- Thousand dollar
rig, brand new.

240
00:08:57,300 --> 00:08:58,200
- Hundred dollars.

241
00:08:59,367 --> 00:09:00,433
- You sure you can
afford it, man?

242
00:09:00,433 --> 00:09:02,800
- [Joel] Okay, I
can't, dickweed!

243
00:09:02,800 --> 00:09:04,400
- That's all right,
man, forget it.

244
00:09:04,400 --> 00:09:07,533
- [Crow] How about if I throw
in dinner and a movie with me?

245
00:09:07,533 --> 00:09:08,867
- [Servo] Twenty dollars.

246
00:09:08,867 --> 00:09:10,433
- Two fifty.

247
00:09:10,433 --> 00:09:11,267
- All right, two fifty.

248
00:09:11,267 --> 00:09:12,100
Do I hear three?

249
00:09:12,100 --> 00:09:13,300
- Four hundred!

250
00:09:13,300 --> 00:09:15,233
- [Servo] Bid four,
bid four fifty.

251
00:09:15,233 --> 00:09:16,633
- It's worth more.

252
00:09:16,633 --> 00:09:17,733
- [Joel] Because I love you!

253
00:09:17,733 --> 00:09:18,700
- Four twenty-five!

254
00:09:19,900 --> 00:09:22,500
- Bless your stingy little hard.

