509
00:18:37,667 --> 00:18:39,633
- [Jeeter] Where
are you staying?

510
00:18:39,633 --> 00:18:41,100
- Nowhere's enough.

511
00:18:41,100 --> 00:18:42,267
- [Crow] Motel 6?

512
00:18:42,267 --> 00:18:43,100
- Well then,

513
00:18:44,433 --> 00:18:46,367
may I give you an invitation

514
00:18:46,367 --> 00:18:49,000
to share our humble chateau?

515
00:18:49,000 --> 00:18:50,500
- [Servo] Your hat?

516
00:18:50,500 --> 00:18:53,600
- [Jeeter] It's not very much
but it's what we call home.

517
00:18:53,600 --> 00:18:56,067
- [Joel] What you call
home, Rambo calls hell.

518
00:18:56,067 --> 00:19:00,433
- My invitation was by no
means extended without reason.

519
00:19:00,433 --> 00:19:03,433
You see, I have a business
proposition to offer you.

520
00:19:03,433 --> 00:19:05,500
Which could mean a lotta bread

521
00:19:05,500 --> 00:19:09,633
and an unlimited expense
account could be yours.

522
00:19:09,633 --> 00:19:12,500
- [Servo] That means security
for you and your loved ones.

523
00:19:12,500 --> 00:19:13,800
- Go ahead, I'm listening.

524
00:19:15,267 --> 00:19:18,400
- This is not the
place nor the time.

525
00:19:18,400 --> 00:19:21,600
Please accept my invitation
to share our humble pad.

526
00:19:22,767 --> 00:19:26,500
- [Servo] Now is it
your pad or your hat?

527
00:19:26,500 --> 00:19:28,367
- [Joel] Will I have to
sleep with the stinky guy?

528
00:19:28,367 --> 00:19:29,200
- Fine.

529
00:19:30,700 --> 00:19:31,800
Linda, baby!

530
00:19:31,800 --> 00:19:32,600
Come here!

531
00:19:32,600 --> 00:19:34,033
- [Joel] You rang?

532
00:19:34,033 --> 00:19:36,200
(Joel growls deeply)

533
00:19:36,200 --> 00:19:38,600
- [Jeeter] Baby, I want
you to meet Rod Tillman.

534
00:19:38,600 --> 00:19:40,500
Rod, say hello to Linda.

535
00:19:40,500 --> 00:19:42,033
- [Crow] You'll be playing
the first round together.

536
00:19:42,033 --> 00:19:44,100
Your category is
world geography.

537
00:19:45,467 --> 00:19:46,700
- Listen, baby,

538
00:19:46,700 --> 00:19:49,333
take my bike and ride
Rod out to our chateau.

539
00:19:49,333 --> 00:19:52,533
- [Servo] Now it's
a chateau again.

540
00:19:52,533 --> 00:19:53,500
- Sure, Jeeter.

541
00:19:54,900 --> 00:19:55,833
- [Joel] Hey, what gives?

542
00:19:55,833 --> 00:19:57,100
- Well aren't you going with us?

543
00:19:57,100 --> 00:19:58,467
- We have

544
00:19:58,467 --> 00:20:01,100
a little unfinished
business to attend to.

545
00:20:01,100 --> 00:20:04,500
- [Crow] Yeah, they got to
go past the La Bianca place.

546
00:20:04,500 --> 00:20:05,733
(out-of-tune guitar chord plays)

547
00:20:05,733 --> 00:20:07,533
- [Joel] Hey, you play
that as well as he does.

548
00:20:07,533 --> 00:20:08,767
- [Crow] Nice guitar.

549
00:20:08,767 --> 00:20:09,600
Not!

550
00:20:14,100 --> 00:20:16,133
- [Joel] Hey, Rod, let
me out of this suitcase!

551
00:20:16,133 --> 00:20:17,400
Please!

552
00:20:17,400 --> 00:20:18,767
For God's sake, let me out!

553
00:20:18,767 --> 00:20:20,767
- [Servo] Oh, I love
meeting new people.

554
00:20:23,100 --> 00:20:24,167
Hey!

555
00:20:24,167 --> 00:20:25,767
It's Jason on the action cam.

556
00:20:27,867 --> 00:20:29,300
- [Linda] Yeah, hop on, baby.

557
00:20:31,533 --> 00:20:32,533
Wango!

558
00:20:32,533 --> 00:20:33,433
- [Crow] Ze tango!

559
00:20:34,600 --> 00:20:36,167
- [Joel] You know, we
gotta find out a way

560
00:20:36,167 --> 00:20:37,967
to sew up the copyright on
those Hell's Angels logos.

561
00:20:37,967 --> 00:20:39,200
These are goin' nowhere.

562
00:20:42,100 --> 00:20:43,033
- I think we oughta

563
00:20:44,200 --> 00:20:46,667
teach those college
creeps a lesson.

564
00:20:46,667 --> 00:20:47,933
- [Crow] Physics or trig?

565
00:20:47,933 --> 00:20:49,833
- [Servo] No, semantical
philosophy, butthead.

566
00:20:58,000 --> 00:20:59,167
- [Crow] Oh, metal shop.

567
00:21:00,100 --> 00:21:03,267
(all laugh menacingly)

568
00:21:07,067 --> 00:21:09,600
- [Joel] Hey, don't let
'em know we got beer, okay?

569
00:21:09,600 --> 00:21:11,000
Be cool.

570
00:21:11,000 --> 00:21:12,800
- [Crow] No, kill the band!

571
00:21:12,800 --> 00:21:14,500
- Hey, creep!

572
00:21:14,500 --> 00:21:15,933
- [Joel] Uh, it's Brandon.

573
00:21:15,933 --> 00:21:17,400
- You talkin' to me?

574
00:21:17,400 --> 00:21:19,500
- You and your friends are
the only creeps in this joint.

575
00:21:20,700 --> 00:21:22,400
- What's going on?

576
00:21:22,400 --> 00:21:24,800
- You enjoy your dance
with our little mama?

577
00:21:24,800 --> 00:21:26,433
- [Servo] That was your mom?

578
00:21:26,433 --> 00:21:28,000
- Look, I just danced with her.

579
00:21:28,000 --> 00:21:29,167
There's no harm done.

580
00:21:29,167 --> 00:21:30,867
- Hey, you don't dig!

581
00:21:30,867 --> 00:21:33,067
Our little mama's
like a virgin goddess.

582
00:21:33,067 --> 00:21:34,800
- [Crow] Well, sorta.

583
00:21:34,800 --> 00:21:36,433
- And no creeps,

584
00:21:36,433 --> 00:21:37,900
no creeps are
allowed to touch her.

585
00:21:37,900 --> 00:21:40,433
- [Crow] Only union
members and their families.

586
00:21:40,433 --> 00:21:42,233
- Hey, these cats are
really way out, aren't they?

587
00:21:42,233 --> 00:21:45,733
- [Joel] They're
totally bonkers!

588
00:21:45,733 --> 00:21:47,167
- Like I said,
there's no harm done.

589
00:21:47,167 --> 00:21:48,133
- Oh, baby.

590
00:21:48,133 --> 00:21:49,767
There's no harm done.

591
00:21:49,767 --> 00:21:51,167
None physically.

592
00:21:51,167 --> 00:21:51,967
Until now!

593
00:21:53,233 --> 00:21:54,300
- [Servo] Check, please!

594
00:21:54,300 --> 00:21:57,267
(grunting)

595
00:21:57,267 --> 00:21:59,733
- [Crow] There's never
a waitress around
when you need one.

596
00:22:01,400 --> 00:22:03,600
- [Servo] Definitely
not gonna tip them now.

597
00:22:04,467 --> 00:22:06,400
(Joel laughing goofily)

598
00:22:06,400 --> 00:22:08,000
- [Joel] Uh, shiny object.

599
00:22:08,000 --> 00:22:08,833
I like it.

600
00:22:11,000 --> 00:22:12,700
- [Servo] Ah! Let's
savor the moments.

601
00:22:12,700 --> 00:22:15,767
- Are you gentlemen
ready for the road?

602
00:22:17,167 --> 00:22:18,400
(Servo laughing goofily)

603
00:22:18,400 --> 00:22:20,700
- Yeah, baby, yeah,
anything you say.

604
00:22:20,700 --> 00:22:25,700
- [Crow] Do we tip 15 or 20%
on a rumble? (chuckles goofily)

605
00:22:26,567 --> 00:22:28,400
- Banjo, baby, lead the way.

606
00:22:30,433 --> 00:22:34,600
(Crow and Servo
laughing goofily)

607
00:22:36,867 --> 00:22:38,600
- [Crow] Tickle, tickle.

608
00:22:38,600 --> 00:22:39,867
Does that bug you?

609
00:22:39,867 --> 00:22:43,633
Does that bug you?
(chuckles goofily)

610
00:22:43,633 --> 00:22:45,567
- [Man] I want my mama.

611
00:22:46,767 --> 00:22:49,400
- [Joel] We're here all
week, enjoy the buffet.

612
00:22:53,567 --> 00:22:54,600
(laughing)

613
00:22:54,600 --> 00:22:56,100
- [Servo] I like
my job too much.

614
00:22:56,100 --> 00:22:58,067
- [Joel] That's the thing
about a job like this.

615
00:22:58,067 --> 00:23:00,133
I never think I have
to go to work tomorrow.

616
00:23:00,133 --> 00:23:01,700
I just love it that much.

617
00:23:01,700 --> 00:23:03,333
- [Crow] Did we
remember to punch out?

618
00:23:03,333 --> 00:23:04,267
I can't remember.

619
00:23:04,267 --> 00:23:05,833
- [Servo] Ah, life.

620
00:23:09,667 --> 00:23:10,567
(engine revving)

621
00:23:10,567 --> 00:23:13,067
- [Joel] Artsy craftsy.

622
00:23:14,600 --> 00:23:16,267
- [Servo] Wow, look at
all those books up there.

623
00:23:16,267 --> 00:23:17,700
- [Crow] Yeah, Leaves of Grass.

624
00:23:17,700 --> 00:23:19,133
- [Joel] Trump: The
Art of the Deal.

625
00:23:19,133 --> 00:23:20,333
- [Servo] Mein Kampf.

626
00:23:20,333 --> 00:23:22,333
- [Crow] The Essays
of Pat Buchanan.

627
00:23:22,333 --> 00:23:23,500
- Bright lights bug me.

628
00:23:24,833 --> 00:23:26,567
This makes everything
much more cozy.

629
00:23:26,567 --> 00:23:27,900
- [Servo] So how long
have you been workin' on

630
00:23:27,900 --> 00:23:29,533
the David Duke's
campaign, honey?

631
00:23:32,133 --> 00:23:34,567
- [Crow] Whoa, those
trees are loud!

632
00:23:34,567 --> 00:23:35,433
- [Servo] Yikes!

633
00:23:35,433 --> 00:23:38,267
(engines revving)

634
00:23:44,533 --> 00:23:47,567
- [Joel] Wow, it sure
is dark out, isn't it?!

635
00:23:47,567 --> 00:23:49,667
- [Servo] Two roads
diverged into a yellow wood,

636
00:23:49,667 --> 00:23:52,833
and sorry I could not
take my heart down both

637
00:23:52,833 --> 00:23:55,400
and be one traveler,
long I stood.

638
00:23:57,133 --> 00:24:00,100
- [Joel] You beat the
stuffing out of three preppies

639
00:24:00,100 --> 00:24:01,400
and given away the girl,

640
00:24:01,400 --> 00:24:03,333
but before the day is through,

641
00:24:03,333 --> 00:24:05,800
you'll take enough
drugs to kill a horse.

642
00:24:05,800 --> 00:24:07,400
Now it's Miller Time.

643
00:24:08,833 --> 00:24:10,967
- [Crow] Guys, it doesn't
get any stupider than this.

644
00:24:12,800 --> 00:24:14,167
- [Joel] Boy, you
know, it's really dark.

645
00:24:14,167 --> 00:24:15,400
- [Servo] Really
dark. Boy, it it dark.

646
00:24:15,400 --> 00:24:17,900
Pitch black out here,
I can't see a thing.

647
00:24:17,900 --> 00:24:18,867
- [Joel] They got
their sunglasses on.

648
00:24:18,867 --> 00:24:19,800
- [Servo] Must be a new moon.

649
00:24:19,800 --> 00:24:21,667
I don't know, it's so dark.

650
00:24:21,667 --> 00:24:23,367
- [Crow] Very
bright for darkness.

651
00:24:24,400 --> 00:24:27,667
(Servo mimics kissing)

652
00:24:28,900 --> 00:24:31,567
- [Servo] Boy, you taste
like Joseph Goebbels.

653
00:24:31,567 --> 00:24:33,467
- Those three bosom buddies
of yours due here any minute,

654
00:24:33,467 --> 00:24:35,667
I want this place
lit up like Broadway.

655
00:24:35,667 --> 00:24:38,133
- [Crow] They say the neon
lights are brighter on Broadway.

656
00:24:38,133 --> 00:24:39,600
- Fantastic.

657
00:24:40,700 --> 00:24:43,700
- Three on one is not much fun.

658
00:24:43,700 --> 00:24:44,700
- [Servo] Says you!

659
00:24:47,800 --> 00:24:50,567
(Joel squeaking)

660
00:24:53,000 --> 00:24:54,667
- [Joel] Orange cappuccino?

661
00:24:54,667 --> 00:24:55,967
Swiss Mocha?

662
00:24:55,967 --> 00:25:00,267
(Crow and Servo
mimic The Penguin)

663
00:25:05,100 --> 00:25:06,800
(Servo sighs)

664
00:25:06,800 --> 00:25:08,700
- [Servo] Celebrate the
moments of your life

665
00:25:08,700 --> 00:25:11,867
with General Foods
International Ripple.

666
00:25:13,467 --> 00:25:14,300
(gang laughs)

667
00:25:14,300 --> 00:25:15,833
We better split, guys.

668
00:25:15,833 --> 00:25:16,767
- [Crow] Okay.

669
00:25:16,767 --> 00:25:17,833
(Servo laughs mockingly)

670
00:25:17,833 --> 00:25:19,200
- [Joel] Oh, for fun!

671
00:25:33,200 --> 00:25:35,467
- Gosh, Joel, that biker
guy sure is sleazy,

672
00:25:35,467 --> 00:25:38,133
but, boy, what a vocabulary!

673
00:25:38,133 --> 00:25:41,700
- Yeah, he's quite eloquent
for a piece of lowlife scum.

674
00:25:41,700 --> 00:25:43,633
- Well you guys might
be surprised to find out

675
00:25:43,633 --> 00:25:45,667
that a lot of the great
thinkers of this century

676
00:25:45,667 --> 00:25:47,467
actually rode in
motorcycle gangs.

677
00:25:47,467 --> 00:25:48,600
In fact I've got
a few drawings--

678
00:25:48,600 --> 00:25:50,033
- Don't tell me.

679
00:25:50,033 --> 00:25:52,100
You've prepared a presentation
using artist renderings.

680
00:25:52,100 --> 00:25:53,700
- Right. You know, you
read me like a book.

681
00:25:53,700 --> 00:25:55,500
And anybody who
reads a lot of books

682
00:25:55,500 --> 00:25:57,867
will know who the
Algonquin Round Table was.

683
00:25:57,867 --> 00:25:59,100
- Well of course.

684
00:25:59,100 --> 00:26:00,933
Alexander Woollcott,
George S. Kaufman,

685
00:26:00,933 --> 00:26:02,933
Robert Benchley, Dorothy Parker.

686
00:26:02,933 --> 00:26:04,800
- Right. Well I've
got this drawing here.

687
00:26:04,800 --> 00:26:06,667
Bring it in a
little bit, Cambot.

688
00:26:06,667 --> 00:26:08,433
Here's the group,
here's their gang.

689
00:26:08,433 --> 00:26:10,833
It's called Satan's Sardonics.

690
00:26:10,833 --> 00:26:13,633
Now, these guys terrorized
the whole East Coast

691
00:26:13,633 --> 00:26:16,200
until one day they were
unexpectedly wiped out

692
00:26:16,200 --> 00:26:18,933
in a rumble with the
cast of What's My Line?

693
00:26:18,933 --> 00:26:20,467
- [Crow] Wow, I guess
that Bennett Cerf

694
00:26:20,467 --> 00:26:21,600
is tougher than people thought!

695
00:26:21,600 --> 00:26:22,833
- [Joel] Yeah.

696
00:26:22,833 --> 00:26:24,533
Now, when you think
of a tough macho rider

697
00:26:24,533 --> 00:26:26,900
who writes in a tense,
hard-boiled style,

698
00:26:26,900 --> 00:26:27,967
who do you think of?

699
00:26:27,967 --> 00:26:28,800
- [Servo] Truman Capote?

700
00:26:28,800 --> 00:26:30,467
- [Joel] Exactly!

701
00:26:30,467 --> 00:26:33,900
See, his gang, Oscar's Wild
Ones, they were leather boys,

702
00:26:33,900 --> 00:26:36,367
were all the range until
Norman Mailer's gang,

703
00:26:36,367 --> 00:26:38,133
Hell's Egos,

704
00:26:38,133 --> 00:26:40,667
mixed it up with
Gore Vidal's gang,

705
00:26:40,667 --> 00:26:42,333
the Vital Sassoons.

706
00:26:42,333 --> 00:26:43,767
- [Crow] Boy,
sounds pretty messy.

707
00:26:43,767 --> 00:26:46,033
"If they don't look good,
we don't look good."

708
00:26:46,033 --> 00:26:48,933
- [Joel] Yeah, there was gel
and mousse for miles around.

709
00:26:48,933 --> 00:26:51,500
The carnage didn't end
until they all joined forces

710
00:26:51,500 --> 00:26:53,100
and finally beat up

711
00:26:54,033 --> 00:26:55,900
Dick Cavett.

712
00:26:55,900 --> 00:26:58,100
- Well, at least we know
all that's in the past now.

713
00:26:58,100 --> 00:26:59,633
- [Joel] Oh, no,
are you kidding?

714
00:26:59,633 --> 00:27:03,667
The intelligentsia's duking it
out on Harleys more even now!

715
00:27:03,667 --> 00:27:04,967
Yeah, sure, check it out.

716
00:27:04,967 --> 00:27:07,100
Here's Ted Koppel's
gang right there.

717
00:27:07,100 --> 00:27:08,667
They're called the Bloods.

718
00:27:08,667 --> 00:27:10,967
Yeah, he's finally the
toughest of them all

719
00:27:10,967 --> 00:27:13,333
'cause they're riding
with Stephen Hawking now.

720
00:27:13,333 --> 00:27:15,567
They beat Bill Moyer's
gang, Moyer's Marauders,

721
00:27:15,567 --> 00:27:17,700
even though Bill rode
with Joseph Campbell.

722
00:27:17,700 --> 00:27:19,500
Everyone though Joseph
Campbell was tough

723
00:27:19,500 --> 00:27:21,733
but that was just a myth.

724
00:27:21,733 --> 00:27:25,033
- Joel, I hope you always
let us ride in your gang.

725
00:27:25,033 --> 00:27:26,500
- Yeah, no problem.

726
00:27:26,500 --> 00:27:28,700
Just so long as you don't
mess with my old lady.

727
00:27:28,700 --> 00:27:31,333
- Oh, fight us off
with a stick, Joel!

728
00:27:31,333 --> 00:27:33,300
(Gypsy cries)

729
00:27:33,300 --> 00:27:34,633
- Oh, that's just great.

730
00:27:34,633 --> 00:27:37,767
Crow, you know she's
especially sensitive right now.

731
00:27:37,767 --> 00:27:38,833
- I'm sorry.

732
00:27:38,833 --> 00:27:40,667
- Dickweed.
- Dickweed.

733
00:27:47,833 --> 00:27:51,133
(gang members laughing)

734
00:27:51,133 --> 00:27:52,367
- [Joel] So you see,

735
00:27:52,367 --> 00:27:53,367
there really are a lot
of brilliant bikers.

736
00:27:53,367 --> 00:27:54,900
- [Servo] It's amazing.

737
00:27:54,900 --> 00:27:56,167
- [Crow] Like these guys.

738
00:27:57,233 --> 00:28:00,467
(Servo slurps, belches)

739
00:28:00,467 --> 00:28:01,933
- [Joel] You know, I feel
a little bit uncomfortable,

740
00:28:01,933 --> 00:28:03,133
but I need to network.

741
00:28:04,867 --> 00:28:09,000
- Nothing like a little
vino to soothe the palate

742
00:28:09,000 --> 00:28:10,300
after a dusty rub.

743
00:28:10,300 --> 00:28:12,367
- [Crow] And da wine
is good too, sir.

744
00:28:14,500 --> 00:28:16,233
- [Joel] Uh, who's
gotta use da helmet?

745
00:28:16,233 --> 00:28:18,100
(Servo laughs goofily)

746
00:28:18,100 --> 00:28:18,933
- Hey, baby.

747
00:28:20,867 --> 00:28:22,633
You remember that
little college banana

748
00:28:22,633 --> 00:28:23,833
you were dancin' with?

749
00:28:23,833 --> 00:28:25,033
- [Servo] Yeah, well
now he's a banana split

750
00:28:25,033 --> 00:28:26,600
with nuts on top.

751
00:28:26,600 --> 00:28:28,100
(Servo laughs goofily, hoots)

752
00:28:28,100 --> 00:28:31,133
- He's missin'
his face. (laughs)

753
00:28:31,133 --> 00:28:32,600
He's missin' his face!

754
00:28:33,867 --> 00:28:34,833
- Now, Banjo.

755
00:28:34,833 --> 00:28:37,400
Such talk will upset our guests.

756
00:28:37,400 --> 00:28:39,300
- [Servo] Ah, room temperature.

757
00:28:39,300 --> 00:28:41,933
- We want nothing
but pleasantries.

758
00:28:41,933 --> 00:28:43,400
- [Crow] Who the hell
are you, Falstaff?

759
00:28:43,400 --> 00:28:44,933
- Let's cut out all
these formalities

760
00:28:44,933 --> 00:28:46,467
and lay the chips on the table.

761
00:28:46,467 --> 00:28:47,300
What's happening?

762
00:28:47,300 --> 00:28:49,000
- [Joel] I love you!

763
00:28:49,000 --> 00:28:52,333
(Jeeter laughs)

764
00:28:52,333 --> 00:28:54,367
- I like this guy,
I really like him.

765
00:28:54,367 --> 00:28:56,700
- He's too square,
baby, a real square.

766
00:28:56,700 --> 00:28:58,233
- Look, you just
keep tryin' to put

767
00:28:58,233 --> 00:28:59,700
that square peg in a round hole

768
00:28:59,700 --> 00:29:01,300
and everything will be fine!

769
00:29:01,300 --> 00:29:03,000
- [Crow] What'd he mean by that?

770
00:29:03,000 --> 00:29:04,533
- Peace.

771
00:29:04,533 --> 00:29:07,267
If we're to be one
big happy family,

772
00:29:07,267 --> 00:29:09,033
we must live in tranquility.

773
00:29:09,033 --> 00:29:10,867
- [Servo] I love it
when he talks this way.

774
00:29:10,867 --> 00:29:11,800
- Okay, Jeeter.

775
00:29:11,800 --> 00:29:13,133
What do you want from me?

776
00:29:14,167 --> 00:29:15,667
- Sit down, Rod.

777
00:29:15,667 --> 00:29:16,900
Relax!

778
00:29:16,900 --> 00:29:18,733
- [Crow] Set a spell,
take your shoes off.

779
00:29:23,700 --> 00:29:25,600
(Servo mimics fart)

780
00:29:25,600 --> 00:29:27,867
- As you might have surmised,

781
00:29:27,867 --> 00:29:31,300
my happy little group
here is from California.

782
00:29:31,300 --> 00:29:32,767
- [Joel] Stanford, right?

783
00:29:32,767 --> 00:29:35,367
- We're strangers to this
Southern countryside.

784
00:29:36,400 --> 00:29:37,233
We need a guide.

785
00:29:38,133 --> 00:29:39,900
A chauffer, if you will.

786
00:29:39,900 --> 00:29:42,500
To drive us around
this countryside

787
00:29:42,500 --> 00:29:43,567
ever so swift.

788
00:29:44,667 --> 00:29:45,500
- It smells.

789
00:29:46,667 --> 00:29:49,167
- [Joel] You're the
stinky guy, right?

790
00:29:49,167 --> 00:29:51,800
- Let Jeeter finish
his epilogue.

791
00:29:51,800 --> 00:29:54,000
- [Crow] Well it's more
of a monologue, really.

792
00:29:54,000 --> 00:29:55,767
- You're right, Rod.

793
00:29:55,767 --> 00:29:56,967
We're bad.

794
00:29:56,967 --> 00:29:58,867
Bad, bad people.

795
00:29:58,867 --> 00:30:01,200
- [Servo] Does he mean
"bad bad" or "good bad"?

796
00:30:01,200 --> 00:30:02,433
- [Crow] Sinbad.

797
00:30:02,433 --> 00:30:04,200
- We do all sorts
of evil things.

798
00:30:04,200 --> 00:30:05,700
- [Crow] We're
opening our own S&L.

799
00:30:05,700 --> 00:30:07,067
- Real kicks!

800
00:30:07,067 --> 00:30:08,400
- [Joel] Yeah, Lucky Charms.

801
00:30:08,400 --> 00:30:09,433
- [Servo] And Honey Comb.

802
00:30:09,433 --> 00:30:10,667
- They're very lucrative.

803
00:30:12,967 --> 00:30:15,400
- Thanks but no thanks.

804
00:30:15,400 --> 00:30:16,900
- Hey, let the man finish.

805
00:30:16,900 --> 00:30:18,400
- [Crow] There's a whole
number he does at the end.

806
00:30:18,400 --> 00:30:20,300
- We need you, man.

807
00:30:20,300 --> 00:30:21,900
- [Joel] Join us.

808
00:30:21,900 --> 00:30:24,100
- We need you real bad.

809
00:30:27,400 --> 00:30:29,267
We're good on bikes,

810
00:30:29,267 --> 00:30:31,767
but cars are a different tale.

811
00:30:31,767 --> 00:30:33,233
- [Servo] Apparently,

812
00:30:33,233 --> 00:30:35,633
they have more wheels on
them or something like that.

813
00:30:35,633 --> 00:30:38,767
- The newspapers told the
story how ya got wiped out.

814
00:30:38,767 --> 00:30:40,900
- [Crow] It's not out yet
but I'm heavily connected.

815
00:30:40,900 --> 00:30:42,333
- Stocks for someone else,

816
00:30:42,333 --> 00:30:43,933
you get peanuts!

817
00:30:43,933 --> 00:30:47,100
- [Servo] But junk bonds, now
they're a different story.

818
00:30:47,100 --> 00:30:48,067
- Bang!

819
00:30:48,067 --> 00:30:51,867
One flameout and that's it.

820
00:30:51,867 --> 00:30:53,633
But with us,

821
00:30:53,633 --> 00:30:54,733
a couple of drives

822
00:30:55,900 --> 00:30:59,500
and it's Moniesville
for a lifetime.

823
00:30:59,500 --> 00:31:03,200
- [Joel] Plus good benefits,
medical, dental, 401(k).

824
00:31:03,200 --> 00:31:04,700
Yeah, I could see
you in the future

825
00:31:04,700 --> 00:31:07,167
with at least four chains on
your right shoulder alone.

826
00:31:08,933 --> 00:31:10,033
- [Crow] Hey, there's
no smoking in here.

827
00:31:10,033 --> 00:31:11,533
- Okay, what do you got in mind?

828
00:31:12,667 --> 00:31:13,600
- An armored car...

829
00:31:13,600 --> 00:31:16,067
- [Servo] An armadillo. (laughs)

830
00:31:16,067 --> 00:31:17,633
- Just like the Roaring '20s.

831
00:31:17,633 --> 00:31:19,067
- [Joel] Only many years later.

832
00:31:19,067 --> 00:31:21,033
- None of that fancy
James Bond stuff.

833
00:31:21,033 --> 00:31:23,000
No secret agent jazz.

834
00:31:23,000 --> 00:31:26,167
Just plain old-fashioned guts.

835
00:31:26,167 --> 00:31:28,767
You know, like Dillinger,
Pretty Boy Floyd...

836
00:31:28,767 --> 00:31:31,300
- [Servo] Michael Milken,
Leona Helmsley, you know.

837
00:31:32,300 --> 00:31:34,000
- What if I refuse?

838
00:31:34,000 --> 00:31:36,967
- [Joel] Well, you get to keep
the girl as our gift to you.

839
00:31:39,367 --> 00:31:40,900
- A lot of kicks, baby.

840
00:31:40,900 --> 00:31:43,033
More kicks than I've
ever dreamed of.

841
00:31:43,033 --> 00:31:45,167
- [Crow] So that
would be about four?

842
00:31:49,633 --> 00:31:52,533
- One question:
what's with fat boy?

843
00:31:52,533 --> 00:31:53,800
- [Servo] Aw, he's got
a thyroid condition.

844
00:31:53,800 --> 00:31:55,067
He can't help his weight.

845
00:31:55,067 --> 00:31:56,867
- The Big Kahuna of
the surfing pack.

846
00:31:56,867 --> 00:31:59,133
And then one day
he got wiped out.

847
00:31:59,133 --> 00:32:01,600
The board caught him
in back of the head.

848
00:32:01,600 --> 00:32:03,300
He ain't never talked since.

849
00:32:03,300 --> 00:32:05,100
- [Crow] Oh, the brains
of the operation.

850
00:32:05,100 --> 00:32:07,267
- We love him just the same.

851
00:32:07,267 --> 00:32:09,167
- [Joel] But he
can't love us back.

852
00:32:10,233 --> 00:32:12,133
- Don't we, Fats?

853
00:32:12,133 --> 00:32:13,933
- [Servo] Shouldn't have
had that Cobb salad.

854
00:32:13,933 --> 00:32:14,767
- Gonna join us?

855
00:32:15,733 --> 00:32:17,467
- [Joel] We're a fun group.

856
00:32:17,467 --> 00:32:18,567
- [Servo] Join us.

857
00:32:18,567 --> 00:32:20,000
- Sorry, friends.

858
00:32:20,967 --> 00:32:22,467
But I like these clothes

859
00:32:22,467 --> 00:32:25,400
and I'm not about to exchange
them for a suit of stripes.

860
00:32:25,400 --> 00:32:26,600
- [Servo] But at
Foreman & Clark,

861
00:32:26,600 --> 00:32:29,367
you can get a second
suit for just a dollar!

862
00:32:29,367 --> 00:32:31,233
- Easy, baby.

863
00:32:31,233 --> 00:32:33,767
- [Crow] Banjo, detune
your G-string, baby.

864
00:32:33,767 --> 00:32:34,800
- Look, Rod.

865
00:32:34,800 --> 00:32:36,033
- [Joel] He hasn't been the same

866
00:32:36,033 --> 00:32:37,733
since the Nitty Gritty
Dirt Band broke up.

867
00:32:37,733 --> 00:32:39,767
- Why all the pickin'
of the brains?

868
00:32:41,167 --> 00:32:42,667
- [Joel] Well, I'm
starting my own company.

869
00:32:42,667 --> 00:32:45,233
- I just wanted to find out
if your offer was legitimate.

870
00:32:46,533 --> 00:32:47,833
- You gonna let him
get away with dis?

871
00:32:47,833 --> 00:32:49,200
- [Crow] Are you
sure it wasn't Banjo

872
00:32:49,200 --> 00:32:50,500
that got the board on
the back of the head?

873
00:32:50,500 --> 00:32:51,833
- [Servo] No, he was
caught for six hours

874
00:32:51,833 --> 00:32:52,900
in a transverse accident.

875
00:32:52,900 --> 00:32:54,733
- I'm a very patient man.

876
00:32:54,733 --> 00:32:56,000
- [Joel] But I hate bank lines.

877
00:32:56,000 --> 00:32:56,800
They bug me.

878
00:32:59,333 --> 00:33:02,767
- Well if that's all,
I guess I'll be going.

879
00:33:05,600 --> 00:33:06,533
- [Servo] (clears throat)

880
00:33:06,533 --> 00:33:08,367
Well, I had a great time.

881
00:33:08,367 --> 00:33:10,533
You'll have to come to my
shotgun shack sometime.

882
00:33:10,533 --> 00:33:12,433
Take care of your
head injuries, guys.

883
00:33:12,433 --> 00:33:14,033
- [Crow] Let's exchange cards.

884
00:33:14,033 --> 00:33:15,367
Contact my people.

885
00:33:15,367 --> 00:33:17,500
- [Jeeter] Banjo, baby!

886
00:33:17,500 --> 00:33:18,867
Where's your manners?

887
00:33:18,867 --> 00:33:22,067
If this man wants
to go, let him.

888
00:33:23,467 --> 00:33:24,900
- Please, baby.

889
00:33:24,900 --> 00:33:26,933
- [Joel] I'll cut your
guitar, man, I will.

890
00:33:26,933 --> 00:33:28,700
I'll cut you a new
sound hole, man.

891
00:33:30,033 --> 00:33:30,967
- He can go!

892
00:33:36,533 --> 00:33:38,300
- [Crow] Uh, well,
uh, thank you then.

893
00:33:38,300 --> 00:33:40,267
It's, uh, been a pleasure.

894
00:33:40,267 --> 00:33:44,433
(Crow chuckles
nervously, whines)

895
00:33:46,533 --> 00:33:48,833
- [Joel] Well let me just say
I wish your business the best

896
00:33:48,833 --> 00:33:50,233
and thanks for all the wine

897
00:33:50,233 --> 00:33:52,267
and the use of your
chick and everything.

898
00:33:55,400 --> 00:33:57,100
- [Crow] That's, uh...

899
00:33:57,100 --> 00:33:58,167
That's the closet.

900
00:33:59,333 --> 00:34:00,600
- [Servo] I hate
these curtains, man!

901
00:34:00,600 --> 00:34:01,667
- Why'd you let
this guy get away--

902
00:34:01,667 --> 00:34:02,567
- You let him in our house--

903
00:34:02,567 --> 00:34:05,567
(mimicking grumbling)

904
00:34:05,567 --> 00:34:06,967
- I said cool it!

905
00:34:06,967 --> 00:34:09,167
- [Crow] What is this,
the McLaughlin Group?

906
00:34:10,567 --> 00:34:11,633
- Our intentions,

907
00:34:12,700 --> 00:34:13,600
not our plans.

908
00:34:16,867 --> 00:34:17,767
- Why'd you let him go?!

909
00:34:17,767 --> 00:34:18,967
- 'Cause he'll be back.

910
00:34:18,967 --> 00:34:20,033
- [Servo] Got his keys. (laughs)

911
00:34:20,033 --> 00:34:21,667
- Just give him a month.

912
00:34:21,667 --> 00:34:22,800
No.

913
00:34:22,800 --> 00:34:24,500
Two weeks.

914
00:34:24,500 --> 00:34:25,667
When he gets hungry,

915
00:34:26,667 --> 00:34:28,300
he'll be back.

916
00:34:28,300 --> 00:34:30,100
- [Joel] Artsy craftsy!

917
00:34:31,233 --> 00:34:32,467
- [Crow] Damn, what
was I thinkin'?

918
00:34:32,467 --> 00:34:33,700
I'll never get a
second interview.

919
00:34:33,700 --> 00:34:35,533
I should send them a
thank you letter though.

920
00:34:35,533 --> 00:34:37,000
Note to myself:

921
00:34:37,000 --> 00:34:39,133
never negotiate with bikers
hopped up on goofballs.

922
00:34:42,867 --> 00:34:43,700
(trumpet sting)

923
00:34:43,700 --> 00:34:44,933
It's showtime!

924
00:34:44,933 --> 00:34:46,200
- [Man] Just hold
it right there.

925
00:34:46,200 --> 00:34:47,200
- [Joel] We've got
Moog synthesizers!

926
00:34:47,200 --> 00:34:48,633
We could kill you from here!

927
00:34:49,967 --> 00:34:51,167
- [Detective] Now
raise your hands.

928
00:34:51,167 --> 00:34:52,900
- [Servo] Now play
a G augmented.

929
00:34:52,900 --> 00:34:54,000
Pat him down.

930
00:34:54,000 --> 00:34:56,033
He's probably packin' a capo.

931
00:34:56,033 --> 00:34:57,500
- He's clean, Lieutenant.

932
00:34:57,500 --> 00:34:59,733
- [Crow] We're booking you
for impersonating Trini Lopez.

933
00:35:00,667 --> 00:35:01,733
- What's your name, kid?

934
00:35:01,733 --> 00:35:04,567
- [Joel] They call me Mr. Tibbs!

935
00:35:04,567 --> 00:35:05,400
- Tillman.

936
00:35:06,567 --> 00:35:07,800
Rod Tillman.

937
00:35:07,800 --> 00:35:10,000
- What are you doin'
up in that cabin?

938
00:35:10,000 --> 00:35:11,233
- [Servo] Oh,
networking, you know.

939
00:35:11,233 --> 00:35:13,133
- I met some characters
at a dance and

940
00:35:14,667 --> 00:35:16,400
they asked me to
come up so I went.

941
00:35:16,400 --> 00:35:17,200
- Why'd you leave?

942
00:35:17,200 --> 00:35:18,400
- [Crow] Lousy benefits.

943
00:35:20,367 --> 00:35:22,033
- We didn't see eye-to-eye
on a few things.

944
00:35:22,033 --> 00:35:23,800
- [Joel] And if they jumped
off a bridge, would you?

945
00:35:23,800 --> 00:35:24,767
- What'd they want?

946
00:35:27,400 --> 00:35:29,167
- Do you mind if I
put my hands down?

947
00:35:29,167 --> 00:35:30,700
- No, that's fine, put 'em down.

948
00:35:30,700 --> 00:35:32,367
- [Servo] Now put 'em
back up again! (laughs)

949
00:35:32,367 --> 00:35:34,033
Didn't say Simon Says. Woo!

950
00:35:38,100 --> 00:35:39,833
- [Joel] Hey, nice caboose.

951
00:35:43,800 --> 00:35:44,633
- [Crow] So, what
you wanna hear?

952
00:35:44,633 --> 00:35:45,900
Melancholy Baby?

953
00:35:47,000 --> 00:35:48,233
Maybe at Sunset?

954
00:35:48,233 --> 00:35:49,467
- Yeah, that sounds good.

955
00:35:49,467 --> 00:35:51,467
- [Servo] Bavarian mint?
You can keep the mug.

956
00:35:52,367 --> 00:35:54,000
- What did they want you for?

957
00:35:54,000 --> 00:35:55,800
- [Joel] Got any of those
little finger sandwiches?

958
00:35:55,800 --> 00:35:57,033
I'm starved.

959
00:35:57,033 --> 00:35:58,667
- I should say an
ex-stock car driver.

960
00:35:59,833 --> 00:36:01,500
And it seems that they
needed a wheel man.

961
00:36:02,600 --> 00:36:03,500
- They're smart.

962
00:36:03,500 --> 00:36:04,500
Real smart.

963
00:36:04,500 --> 00:36:06,033
- [Joel] Yep.

964
00:36:06,033 --> 00:36:07,967
- They know we can spot those
motorcycles before a robbery,

965
00:36:07,967 --> 00:36:09,533
so now they're gonna
switch to a car.

966
00:36:09,533 --> 00:36:10,967
- [Servo] Yeah, cars
are harder to see.

967
00:36:10,967 --> 00:36:13,100
- If you know they're stealin',
why don't you arrest them?

968
00:36:13,100 --> 00:36:14,300
- We have.

969
00:36:14,300 --> 00:36:15,967
No witnesses, no evidence.

970
00:36:15,967 --> 00:36:18,467
- [Joel] No jail, no
handcuffs, nothin'.

971
00:36:18,467 --> 00:36:19,300
- How come?

972
00:36:19,300 --> 00:36:20,667
- Well as I say,

973
00:36:20,667 --> 00:36:21,900
they're smart.

974
00:36:21,900 --> 00:36:24,133
They get rid of their
guns after each job.

975
00:36:24,133 --> 00:36:26,467
- [Servo] Oh, look, they're
just really smart, okay?

976
00:36:26,467 --> 00:36:27,967
- They certainly don't live big.

977
00:36:29,600 --> 00:36:31,167
It's almost as though they're

978
00:36:31,167 --> 00:36:32,867
robbin' just for
the thrill of it.

979
00:36:34,000 --> 00:36:35,333
- Kicks.

980
00:36:35,333 --> 00:36:36,367
Only for kicks.

981
00:36:36,367 --> 00:36:37,967
- What'd you say?

982
00:36:37,967 --> 00:36:39,533
- [Joel] It's a cereal, man!

983
00:36:39,533 --> 00:36:40,467
Really good!

984
00:36:40,467 --> 00:36:41,767
- They're only in it for kicks!

985
00:36:42,933 --> 00:36:44,700
- Do you think you could
gain their confidence?

986
00:36:44,700 --> 00:36:47,267
- [Crow] Look, you're
not a real cop, are you?

987
00:36:47,267 --> 00:36:50,633
- Let's say that we didn't
leave the best of friends.

988
00:36:50,633 --> 00:36:51,800
- Did they seem...

989
00:36:51,800 --> 00:36:53,067
- [Joel] Smart?

990
00:36:53,067 --> 00:36:54,933
- Disappointed when you
wouldn't drive for them?

991
00:36:54,933 --> 00:36:56,400
- [Servo] They're really
close to the breast.

992
00:36:56,400 --> 00:36:58,500
- Yeah, I think they
needed me real bad.

993
00:36:58,500 --> 00:36:59,500
- [Crow] They cried.

994
00:37:00,433 --> 00:37:01,700
- Look, Rod, I got a plan.

995
00:37:02,600 --> 00:37:04,600
Now, if it works out,

996
00:37:04,600 --> 00:37:07,433
would you be willin' to work
for us, work for the police?

997
00:37:07,433 --> 00:37:09,167
- [Servo] (gasps)
If you'd have me!

998
00:37:10,300 --> 00:37:12,400
- [Joel] It's called
Operation Weasel Snitch.

999
00:37:14,033 --> 00:37:14,867
- Maybe.

1000
00:37:15,867 --> 00:37:16,700
Tell me more.

1001
00:37:23,133 --> 00:37:26,333
- [Servo] Lieutenant,
you have lovely feet!

1002
00:37:26,333 --> 00:37:28,433
- [Crow] It's Joe Namath!

1003
00:37:28,433 --> 00:37:29,967
Oh. No.

1004
00:37:29,967 --> 00:37:32,000
- [Joel] Oh no,
it's Marsha Brady,

1005
00:37:32,000 --> 00:37:34,967
all grown up and
back from college.

1006
00:37:34,967 --> 00:37:36,433
(Servo growls)

