Bruce Wayne's house?

1249
00:47:36,033 --> 00:47:38,733
Say, he's not bad!

1250
00:47:41,133 --> 00:47:43,167
Oh, that's me.

1251
00:47:43,167 --> 00:47:44,000
Excuse me.

1252
00:47:45,633 --> 00:47:48,033
- [Servo] Are they
robbing a bait shop?

1253
00:47:48,033 --> 00:47:49,500
- [Crow] Hmm, Winchester 408,

1254
00:47:49,500 --> 00:47:52,667
200-grain bullet with 2400 feet
per second muzzle velocity,

1255
00:47:52,667 --> 00:47:54,667
and an incredibly
fragged trajectory.

1256
00:47:54,667 --> 00:47:56,433
High powered rifle. Like.

1257
00:47:56,433 --> 00:47:58,400
- [Joel] This must
be where the South

1258
00:47:58,400 --> 00:48:00,167
bought all the stuff
for the Civil War.

1259
00:48:00,167 --> 00:48:03,500
- [Servo] And the
Spanish-American War
and the War of 1812.

1260
00:48:03,500 --> 00:48:06,467
- [Crow] Oh, Paul, have you
ever robbed a bait shop?

1261
00:48:06,467 --> 00:48:08,533
- [Joel] Ah, I don't
think so, Dave.

1262
00:48:12,567 --> 00:48:13,867
- Good morning, may I help you?

1263
00:48:13,867 --> 00:48:16,067
- Why, yes you may.

1264
00:48:16,067 --> 00:48:18,167
We've been bothered
by prowlers lately.

1265
00:48:18,167 --> 00:48:20,267
And with my husband
out of town...

1266
00:48:20,267 --> 00:48:22,633
- [Servo] (laughs) Nothing
like the wily charms

1267
00:48:22,633 --> 00:48:25,933
of an attractive woman to
get an old man off his guard.

1268
00:48:25,933 --> 00:48:27,633
- With all the unsavory
people in the world today,

1269
00:48:27,633 --> 00:48:29,267
you need protection.

1270
00:48:29,267 --> 00:48:31,233
- [Crow] Yes, yes, yes!

1271
00:48:31,233 --> 00:48:33,567
- What kind of gun
did you have in mind?

1272
00:48:33,567 --> 00:48:37,100
- I'm going to leave
that 100% up to you.

1273
00:48:37,100 --> 00:48:40,467
- [Joel] Wow, check out the
Ray Kroc death mask up there.

1274
00:48:42,833 --> 00:48:45,000
- [Servo] Now, this is the
one Ruby used to shoot Oswald.

1275
00:48:45,000 --> 00:48:47,033
- This is a very popular
model with the ladies.

1276
00:48:47,033 --> 00:48:50,300
- If you recommend it, I'm
sure it will suit my purpose.

1277
00:48:51,167 --> 00:48:52,967
Can you show me how it works?

1278
00:48:52,967 --> 00:48:54,200
- Surely.

1279
00:48:54,200 --> 00:48:55,567
- [Crow] Okay, stand
against that wall.

1280
00:48:55,567 --> 00:48:56,733
- You insert the clip.

1281
00:48:56,733 --> 00:48:58,200
Like this.

1282
00:48:58,200 --> 00:49:00,367
- [Servo] Thrusting it
manfully into the chamber.

1283
00:49:00,367 --> 00:49:01,533
- Like this.

1284
00:49:01,533 --> 00:49:03,433
See, this puts a bullet
up in the chamber.

1285
00:49:03,433 --> 00:49:04,900
Then all you have to
do is... (gun clicks)

1286
00:49:04,900 --> 00:49:06,033
pull the trigger.

1287
00:49:06,033 --> 00:49:07,800
Here, you try it.

1288
00:49:07,800 --> 00:49:08,900
- [Crow] Try it on me.

1289
00:49:10,733 --> 00:49:12,767
- This is the safety.

1290
00:49:15,633 --> 00:49:16,467
- I see now.

1291
00:49:19,833 --> 00:49:21,400
You put on the safety.

1292
00:49:22,433 --> 00:49:23,600
Then pull the trigger.

1293
00:49:23,600 --> 00:49:24,533
- [Joel] Wrong!

1294
00:49:24,533 --> 00:49:26,300
- No, first you put in the clip.

1295
00:49:26,300 --> 00:49:27,800
- Oh, first the clip.

1296
00:49:28,833 --> 00:49:30,000
- You're putting
it in backwards.

1297
00:49:30,000 --> 00:49:31,533
Let me help you.

1298
00:49:31,533 --> 00:49:33,400
(Crow quivers)

1299
00:49:33,400 --> 00:49:34,667
- [Joel] Oh, wow.

1300
00:49:34,667 --> 00:49:36,400
- [Crow] What is this, a
Shed Spread commercial?

1301
00:49:36,400 --> 00:49:37,733
- I'll take it.

1302
00:49:37,733 --> 00:49:40,200
- That'll be 79.95,

1303
00:49:40,200 --> 00:49:41,767
plus tax.

1304
00:49:41,767 --> 00:49:43,067
- I'll need some bullets.

1305
00:49:44,367 --> 00:49:46,333
- [Servo] This is my
rifle, this is my gun.

1306
00:49:46,333 --> 00:49:47,733
One is for retail,

1307
00:49:47,733 --> 00:49:49,067
the other's for fun.

1308
00:49:49,067 --> 00:49:50,767
- [Crow] Yes, yes,
yes! She likes me!

1309
00:49:50,767 --> 00:49:52,400
She likes me, she's buying it!

1310
00:49:52,400 --> 00:49:53,933
Don't screw it up, okay, calm.

1311
00:49:54,833 --> 00:49:55,767
She's buying it!

1312
00:49:55,767 --> 00:49:58,600
(giggles, clears throat)

1313
00:49:58,600 --> 00:50:00,933
- I'll throw these in as
a gift from the house.

1314
00:50:00,933 --> 00:50:03,933
- [Servo] And you get
the sneaker phone too!

1315
00:50:03,933 --> 00:50:06,433
- Would you mind
loading the gun for me?

1316
00:50:06,433 --> 00:50:07,667
(Joel grimaces)

1317
00:50:07,667 --> 00:50:09,900
- How stupid of me.

1318
00:50:09,900 --> 00:50:11,900
- [Crow] He's
loading it. (quivers)

1319
00:50:11,900 --> 00:50:13,933
- [Joel] Very interesting.

1320
00:50:13,933 --> 00:50:14,767
- [Servo] Hogan!

1321
00:50:16,100 --> 00:50:17,033
- Relax.

1322
00:50:17,033 --> 00:50:17,867
- [Servo] Schultz!

1323
00:50:17,867 --> 00:50:19,033
- She's a born actress.

1324
00:50:19,033 --> 00:50:19,867
- [Crow] She's no Streep.

1325
00:50:19,867 --> 00:50:20,900
- She's performing.

1326
00:50:22,533 --> 00:50:24,100
- There we are.

1327
00:50:24,100 --> 00:50:26,567
Always remember to
keep the safety on.

1328
00:50:26,567 --> 00:50:28,400
- [Crow] And if you can't
remember, name it after me.

1329
00:50:28,400 --> 00:50:29,900
(laughs nervously)

1330
00:50:29,900 --> 00:50:31,433
A little gun shop joke.

1331
00:50:32,800 --> 00:50:35,433
- Let me get you a nice
box to wrap that in.

1332
00:50:35,433 --> 00:50:37,633
- [Servo] (clears throat) Crow?

1333
00:50:37,633 --> 00:50:39,000
- [Joel] I'd like to
return these bullets

1334
00:50:39,000 --> 00:50:40,933
to their original owner.

1335
00:50:40,933 --> 00:50:42,500
- First rule of gun safety.

1336
00:50:42,500 --> 00:50:45,133
You never point a gun at anyone.

1337
00:50:45,133 --> 00:50:47,600
- Not even if you're
going to rob them?

1338
00:50:47,600 --> 00:50:48,633
- [Servo] No, not
even you're go... huh?

1339
00:50:48,633 --> 00:50:49,600
- I beg your pardon?

1340
00:50:49,600 --> 00:50:51,133
- Just do what I tell you

1341
00:50:51,133 --> 00:50:53,867
and you'll live to tell your
wife this shocking experience.

1342
00:50:53,867 --> 00:50:55,900
- Now just a minute--

1343
00:50:55,900 --> 00:50:58,467
- [Joel] Sounds like she
shot him with a staple gun.

1344
00:50:59,633 --> 00:51:01,567
- [Servo] Banjo, quit
playing yourself!

1345
00:51:01,567 --> 00:51:02,400
Come on!

1346
00:51:04,933 --> 00:51:07,600
- [Joel] Man, I wish these
clowns would learn to wash.

1347
00:51:07,600 --> 00:51:10,433
They always play the
radio too loud, too.

1348
00:51:10,433 --> 00:51:11,367
- [Crow] I'll, uh...

1349
00:51:11,367 --> 00:51:12,500
I'll just wait here then, huh?

1350
00:51:14,800 --> 00:51:16,667
- [Servo] Yee-hoo!

1351
00:51:16,667 --> 00:51:19,300
- [Crow] Hey, he looks like
Michael Caine in Zulu Dawn!

1352
00:51:20,667 --> 00:51:21,900
- [Banjo] This place is
gonna make us righteous, man!

1353
00:51:21,900 --> 00:51:22,733
Look at it!

1354
00:51:24,367 --> 00:51:25,200
- Oh ho!

1355
00:51:26,167 --> 00:51:28,667
Wait'll you see what I've got!

1356
00:51:31,033 --> 00:51:33,733
- [Servo] Clean up in
aisle three, please.

1357
00:51:33,733 --> 00:51:34,967
- [Crow] Oh! Ouch!

1358
00:51:34,967 --> 00:51:36,700
Oh, you gotta be
careful doin' that.

1359
00:51:38,533 --> 00:51:40,400
- [Joel] We're gonna
need a car here.

1360
00:51:41,500 --> 00:51:43,967
(Fats chuckling maniacally)

1361
00:51:43,967 --> 00:51:47,933
(Servo mimicking laughter)

1362
00:51:47,933 --> 00:51:50,400
- [Servo] Let's watch as
Benny Hill buys a gun.

1363
00:51:51,967 --> 00:51:53,933
- [Joel] I love you.
I really love you.

1364
00:51:55,633 --> 00:51:57,600
- [Crow] Uh, they do
have bullets there.

1365
00:52:01,300 --> 00:52:03,633
- Hey, what do you got, Banjo?

1366
00:52:03,633 --> 00:52:05,333
- [Servo] It's
called a gun, dear.

1367
00:52:06,367 --> 00:52:07,900
(grunting)

1368
00:52:07,900 --> 00:52:10,367
- [Joel] You know, I think
he's funnier than Benny Hill.

1369
00:52:10,367 --> 00:52:11,567
- [Servo] Definitely.

1370
00:52:11,567 --> 00:52:13,033
- [Crow] Blue light
special on chromosomes.

1371
00:52:13,033 --> 00:52:13,867
Extra ones.

1372
00:52:14,867 --> 00:52:16,900
- Come on, let's go!

1373
00:52:16,900 --> 00:52:19,133
- Okay, come on,
let's get outta here!

1374
00:52:19,133 --> 00:52:21,167
- [Crow] Not the hat, it
makes you look stupid.

1375
00:52:21,167 --> 00:52:23,767
- Come on, let's go!

1376
00:52:23,767 --> 00:52:26,000
Move it, come on, let's go!

1377
00:52:26,000 --> 00:52:28,533
- [Joel] Come on, ten
items or less, let's go.

1378
00:52:32,200 --> 00:52:34,400
- [Servo] Well, at least
they're not concealed weapons.

1379
00:52:34,400 --> 00:52:35,967
They'd get in trouble for that.

1380
00:52:41,300 --> 00:52:42,533
A modest assortment.

1381
00:52:42,533 --> 00:52:44,600
- Banjo, Fats, get
some ammunition.

1382
00:52:44,600 --> 00:52:46,067
- [Crow] How they gonna remember
what kinda guns they got?

1383
00:52:46,067 --> 00:52:48,867
- [Servo] This is the movies,
Crow, bullets are bullets.

1384
00:52:50,400 --> 00:52:52,300
- Just relax, baby.

1385
00:52:52,300 --> 00:52:53,733
It'll only be a minute.

1386
00:52:53,733 --> 00:52:55,233
- We need bullets!

1387
00:52:55,233 --> 00:52:55,800
How are we gonna kill
anybody without 'em, huh?

1388
00:52:57,767 --> 00:53:00,067
- [Crow] Kind of a
pre-shooting shopping spree.

1389
00:53:00,067 --> 00:53:01,733
- [Servo] Looks like...

1390
00:53:01,733 --> 00:53:02,567
Lunch!

1391
00:53:09,233 --> 00:53:12,167
- [Joel] Red ones and red
ones and red ones and...

1392
00:53:22,333 --> 00:53:23,833
- [Crow] Love me...

1393
00:53:23,833 --> 00:53:25,333
Thank you very much.

1394
00:53:25,333 --> 00:53:27,800
Now I'm gonna have a peanut
butter and nana sandwich.

1395
00:53:29,833 --> 00:53:32,433
- [Joel] Wonder if he knows
London Bridge is Falling Down.

1396
00:53:32,433 --> 00:53:34,100
- [Servo] Yeah, and
The Girl from Ipanema.

1397
00:53:37,267 --> 00:53:38,600
- [Crow] Thank you, I call
that the Devil's Tritone.

1398
00:53:38,600 --> 00:53:40,567
People go crazy for it.

1399
00:53:40,567 --> 00:53:42,733
- [Joel] Is this
bugging you guys?

1400
00:53:42,733 --> 00:53:45,267
I mean just let me know
if it's bugging you.

1401
00:53:45,267 --> 00:53:48,800
Tends to annoy some people
sometimes and I find that I...

1402
00:53:48,800 --> 00:53:49,933
I don't know.

1403
00:53:49,933 --> 00:53:51,400
Is that bugging you?

1404
00:53:51,400 --> 00:53:53,300
- I said cool it!

1405
00:53:53,300 --> 00:53:54,500
- [Servo] I don't know that one,

1406
00:53:54,500 --> 00:53:56,467
but this one's called
Put a Sock In It.

1407
00:53:56,467 --> 00:53:58,800
- I think it's best
if you both cooled it.

1408
00:53:58,800 --> 00:54:00,567
- He's making me nervous
with that git fiddle.

1409
00:54:00,567 --> 00:54:02,000
- Sit down.

1410
00:54:02,000 --> 00:54:03,100
- [Crow] I mean, it's
pretty and all but quit it.

1411
00:54:03,100 --> 00:54:03,933
- Sit down.

1412
00:54:05,200 --> 00:54:08,000
- [Joel] Hey, get that
shotgun to sing a song.

1413
00:54:08,000 --> 00:54:09,100
- [Jeeter] Can the music?

1414
00:54:09,100 --> 00:54:10,233
- [Crow] Canned music?

1415
00:54:10,233 --> 00:54:11,633
No way, I'm an
artist, I have values!

1416
00:54:19,600 --> 00:54:20,600
- Thank you.

1417
00:54:22,600 --> 00:54:23,433
Look, cats.

1418
00:54:24,533 --> 00:54:25,933
Now that we got our arsenal,

1419
00:54:27,667 --> 00:54:30,167
it's gonna be Kicksville
from here on out.

1420
00:54:30,167 --> 00:54:32,433
- [Crow] I'm being
transferred to Kicksville?

1421
00:54:33,600 --> 00:54:35,600
- Go get me those
layouts you drew up.

1422
00:54:35,600 --> 00:54:37,100
- [Joel] On the laser printer.

1423
00:54:38,367 --> 00:54:39,467
Ouch, owie.

1424
00:54:41,467 --> 00:54:42,300
Too tight.

1425
00:54:42,300 --> 00:54:45,633
(Crow mimics squeaking)

1426
00:54:49,067 --> 00:54:50,300
(Joel sneezes)

1427
00:54:50,300 --> 00:54:51,333
- [Joel] Excuse me.

1428
00:54:51,333 --> 00:54:52,733
- [Crow] Gesundheit.

1429
00:54:52,733 --> 00:54:54,533
- [Joel] There's Don
Ho's jacket up there.

1430
00:54:54,533 --> 00:54:56,233
- [Servo] Let's see: "We
hold these truths to..."

1431
00:54:56,233 --> 00:54:57,500
Wait a minute, this isn't right.

1432
00:54:57,500 --> 00:54:58,767
- When you guys
have been takin' in

1433
00:54:58,767 --> 00:55:00,333
all that sack time
in the afternoon.

1434
00:55:00,333 --> 00:55:02,233
- [Crow] I've been taking
a correspondence course.

1435
00:55:02,233 --> 00:55:05,367
- I've had our little
actress here out performing.

1436
00:55:06,800 --> 00:55:09,700
She cased some pads that
are filled with more bread

1437
00:55:09,700 --> 00:55:11,333
than you ever dreamed existed.

1438
00:55:11,333 --> 00:55:13,733
- [Servo] Whoa, that's a
lotta slang for one sentence.

1439
00:55:13,733 --> 00:55:15,433
- You're outta sight, baby.

1440
00:55:15,433 --> 00:55:17,200
- [Joel] Well you better
put your bifocals in.

1441
00:55:17,200 --> 00:55:18,367
- Real, real righteous.

1442
00:55:19,267 --> 00:55:22,933
(Servo mimics deep kissing)

1443
00:55:27,533 --> 00:55:29,100
- [Crow] Banjo, I
believe you're next.

1444
00:55:29,100 --> 00:55:30,300
Fatty, wait your turn.

1445
00:55:32,033 --> 00:55:35,267
- Now if my little flock
will gather round...

1446
00:55:35,267 --> 00:55:38,100
(Crow and Servo mimic sheep)

1447
00:55:38,100 --> 00:55:39,333
- [Joel] Will I ever be
as smart as that guy?

1448
00:55:39,333 --> 00:55:40,867
I just don't think so.

1449
00:55:40,867 --> 00:55:42,933
I don't think I'll do it.

1450
00:55:45,233 --> 00:55:46,700
- [Crow] Boss,

1451
00:55:46,700 --> 00:55:48,533
I made some bars but I can't
get the oven to preheat.

1452
00:55:48,533 --> 00:55:49,967
Can you help me?

1453
00:55:50,900 --> 00:55:52,733
- He's outta sight, baby.

1454
00:55:52,733 --> 00:55:53,567
He's okay.

1455
00:55:53,567 --> 00:55:54,767
- Why take a chance?

1456
00:55:54,767 --> 00:55:56,000
- [Servo] He's in
plain sight, I think.

1457
00:55:56,000 --> 00:55:57,367
- We can brief him
on the way tomorrow.

1458
00:55:57,367 --> 00:55:58,400
He's only the driver.

1459
00:56:01,500 --> 00:56:02,300
- Rod.

1460
00:56:02,300 --> 00:56:03,733
- [Servo] Rod,

1461
00:56:03,733 --> 00:56:04,667
we need a few more people
nibbling on me here.

1462
00:56:04,667 --> 00:56:05,800
Come on over.

1463
00:56:06,933 --> 00:56:09,567
- Go out and serenade the moon.

1464
00:56:09,567 --> 00:56:11,300
- [Joel] Wear a necktie
so I know it's you.

1465
00:56:11,300 --> 00:56:13,233
- What's the matter,
don't you trust me?

1466
00:56:13,233 --> 00:56:14,767
- Let's just say...

1467
00:56:14,767 --> 00:56:15,600
- [All] No.

1468
00:56:15,600 --> 00:56:17,567
- Security precautions.

1469
00:56:17,567 --> 00:56:19,367
- [Crow] Okay,
security precautions.

1470
00:56:19,367 --> 00:56:20,967
Give us another one, that's fun.

1471
00:56:22,867 --> 00:56:24,333
- Okay, it's your race.

1472
00:56:26,067 --> 00:56:27,433
- [Joel] White Nazi race.

1473
00:56:34,900 --> 00:56:37,100
- But if I'm gonna
be the driver,

1474
00:56:37,100 --> 00:56:38,567
you're gonna have to
tell me what's happening.

1475
00:56:38,567 --> 00:56:40,167
- [Joel] Well there's a
steering wheel and a pedal...

1476
00:56:40,167 --> 00:56:42,300
Oh, would you just
get out of here!

1477
00:56:42,300 --> 00:56:43,900
Crazy kooky-head.

1478
00:56:45,933 --> 00:56:47,600
- That square bugs me!

1479
00:56:48,867 --> 00:56:50,333
He really bugs me!

1480
00:56:50,333 --> 00:56:51,833
- [Crow] We're here,
man, let it out.

1481
00:56:51,833 --> 00:56:53,633
- Don't let him bug ya, baby.

1482
00:56:53,633 --> 00:56:56,067
- [Crow] See this
shoulder, it's here for ya.

1483
00:56:56,067 --> 00:56:57,233
- For a while.

1484
00:56:58,833 --> 00:57:00,533
- [Joel] Eat. Eat, Fatty.

1485
00:57:00,533 --> 00:57:02,533
- Go outside and
keep your eye on him.

1486
00:57:02,533 --> 00:57:05,733
- [Servo] Which one?
(laughs goofily)

1487
00:57:07,067 --> 00:57:07,900
- No, Fats.

1488
00:57:09,333 --> 00:57:10,767
On second thought,

1489
00:57:11,700 --> 00:57:13,500
Linda, you go out and watch him.

1490
00:57:13,500 --> 00:57:14,767
It won't be so obvious, baby.

1491
00:57:14,767 --> 00:57:17,267
- Just let me comb my hair

1492
00:57:17,267 --> 00:57:19,500
and I'll be on him
like a bloodhound.

1493
00:57:19,500 --> 00:57:22,667
(Crow and Servo howl)

1494
00:57:23,967 --> 00:57:24,833
- [Joel] Aqualung!

1495
00:57:24,833 --> 00:57:26,333
- [Crow] Freebird!

1496
00:57:28,633 --> 00:57:29,867
- [Joel] Hey,
that's a pretty good

1497
00:57:29,867 --> 00:57:31,600
G. Gordon Liddy
impression there.

1498
00:57:32,900 --> 00:57:34,533
- [Servo] Meanwhile,
in Africa...

1499
00:57:41,933 --> 00:57:43,200
- [Joel] Let's see,

1500
00:57:43,200 --> 00:57:46,133
if you are not wearing
any underwear, smile.

1501
00:57:49,100 --> 00:57:50,067
- [Crow] Underwear?

1502
00:57:52,700 --> 00:57:55,300
- [Servo] Note to
myself: get new agent.

1503
00:57:57,700 --> 00:57:58,533
Thank you.

1504
00:58:03,067 --> 00:58:04,700
- [Joel] What's he gonna do?

1505
00:58:04,700 --> 00:58:06,900
- [Crow] Fold it so
no one can read it.

1506
00:58:06,900 --> 00:58:08,100
- [Servo] And then...

1507
00:58:08,100 --> 00:58:08,933
Huh?

1508
00:58:10,900 --> 00:58:13,167
- [Crow] Oh, he's sending
it by carrier vole.

1509
00:58:19,733 --> 00:58:22,400
- [Joel] I've...
hidden... the note.

1510
00:58:22,400 --> 00:58:24,933
- [Servo] We'll be back with
Peek-a-Boo Siding Showcase

1511
00:58:24,933 --> 00:58:26,900
but first (chuckles)

1512
00:58:26,900 --> 00:58:27,733
a little of her.

1513
00:58:31,567 --> 00:58:32,400
- [Servo] Quick.

1514
00:58:32,400 --> 00:58:33,233
- [Crow] Think fast.

1515
00:58:33,233 --> 00:58:34,500
This'll fool her.

1516
00:58:34,500 --> 00:58:35,933
(chuckles)

1517
00:58:35,933 --> 00:58:37,500
- There's the signal now.

1518
00:58:37,500 --> 00:58:38,733
Run up and get the message.

1519
00:58:38,733 --> 00:58:39,967
- [Servo] Ooh, but it
might be dangerous!

1520
00:58:42,067 --> 00:58:44,133
- [Joel] Ouch. Sting-y.

1521
00:58:44,133 --> 00:58:46,200
- [Crow] She must go
through a lot of pants.

1522
00:58:46,200 --> 00:58:49,533
(Joel mimics squeaking)

1523
00:58:51,367 --> 00:58:52,533
- Hold it. Hold it, Bob.

1524
00:58:52,533 --> 00:58:53,767
- [Crow] Hold what?

1525
00:58:53,767 --> 00:58:54,700
- [Servo] Now hold
it up to the light.

1526
00:58:54,700 --> 00:58:55,800
- Looks like Rod's got company.

1527
00:58:58,967 --> 00:58:59,900
- [Crow] Uh oh.

1528
00:58:59,900 --> 00:59:01,200
Love me tender, love me sweet.

1529
00:59:01,200 --> 00:59:02,600
Thank you very much.

1530
00:59:02,600 --> 00:59:05,267
Elvis has left the theater.

1531
00:59:05,267 --> 00:59:07,067
- [Joel] He's sending
another message now.

1532
00:59:07,067 --> 00:59:09,600
- [Servo] It's a
musical message of love.

1533
00:59:12,533 --> 00:59:14,633
- You're quite the
troubadour, aren't you?

1534
00:59:14,633 --> 00:59:16,500
- [Joel] Yeah, and
I play guitar too!

1535
00:59:17,933 --> 00:59:20,767
- Just a roving minstrel
at your service, me lady.

1536
00:59:20,767 --> 00:59:21,700
- Play on.

1537
00:59:21,700 --> 00:59:22,633
- [Crow] McDuff.

1538
00:59:22,633 --> 00:59:23,967
- What would you like to hear?

1539
00:59:23,967 --> 00:59:25,600
- [Linda] Whatever
strikes your fancy.

1540
00:59:25,600 --> 00:59:28,667
- [Servo] Personally, I
like guys in clown suits.

1541
00:59:28,667 --> 00:59:30,100
(Rod plays guitar)

1542
00:59:30,100 --> 00:59:31,967
- [Joel] Oh, the
Wango Ze Tango, huh?

1543
00:59:34,133 --> 00:59:36,300
- [Servo] Nothing like
a moonlit afternoon.

1544
00:59:39,333 --> 00:59:43,000
(all sing like Jerry Lewis)

1545
00:59:49,633 --> 00:59:54,633
♪ 'Cause I like what I know ♪

1546
00:59:55,267 --> 00:59:56,800
♪ About you ♪

1547
00:59:56,800 --> 00:59:58,967
- [Joel] What a jerk.

1548
00:59:58,967 --> 01:00:01,200
- [Crow] Looks like
Frank Sinatra, Jr.

1549
01:00:01,200 --> 01:00:02,400
(horn plays)

1550
01:00:02,400 --> 01:00:04,500
Thank you, brother
squirrel, for the horn.

1551
01:00:08,067 --> 01:00:11,200
- [Joel] Special music by
the Ant Farm Family Singers.

1552
01:00:13,167 --> 01:00:14,600
- [Servo] Good thing
the Nelson Riddle gang

1553
01:00:14,600 --> 01:00:16,333
is in the next cottage.

1554
01:00:17,733 --> 01:00:19,200
- [Crow] Maybe I can kill
him with a cigarette.

1555
01:00:21,200 --> 01:00:22,333
- [Joel] Do some backup.

1556
01:00:22,333 --> 01:00:25,267
(Servo scats bass)

1557
01:00:29,700 --> 01:00:31,600
♪ But I still know nothing ♪

1558
01:00:31,600 --> 01:00:33,000
- [Crow] Take it, chipmunks!

1559
01:00:35,800 --> 01:00:38,467
♪ About your secret charm ♪

1560
01:00:38,467 --> 01:00:40,767
- [Joel] (sighs) I hope
this isn't a long song.

1561
01:00:42,967 --> 01:00:45,000
♪ 'Cause I've never kissed you ♪

1562
01:00:45,000 --> 01:00:47,767
- [Crow] This is a cover of
an old Kristie Weasel song.

1563
01:00:49,400 --> 01:00:50,567
- [Joel] New Kristie Weasels?

1564
01:00:50,567 --> 01:00:51,833
- [Crow] Yep.

1565
01:00:51,833 --> 01:00:52,767
- [Servo] I thought it
was Up with Weasels.

1566
01:00:57,633 --> 01:00:59,000
You talkin' to me?

1567
01:00:59,000 --> 01:01:01,200
♪ One night I will ♪

1568
01:01:01,200 --> 01:01:03,767
(Servo swoons)

1569
01:01:04,933 --> 01:01:05,867
- [Servo] Carried away.

1570
01:01:05,867 --> 01:01:07,400
- [Crow] My god, are you okay?

1571
01:01:09,267 --> 01:01:10,400
- [Servo] Little
B.J. Thomas there.

1572
01:01:10,400 --> 01:01:13,967
♪ Then I love ♪

1573
01:01:13,967 --> 01:01:15,900
♪ What I know ♪

1574
01:01:15,900 --> 01:01:18,367
- [Servo] A little
flat there, squirrels.

1575
01:01:18,367 --> 01:01:20,533
♪ About ♪

1576
01:01:20,533 --> 01:01:22,367
♪ You ♪

1577
01:01:26,300 --> 01:01:28,967
- [Crow] This must be
the B side of the 45.

1578
01:01:31,600 --> 01:01:32,833
Next, thank you!

1579
01:01:32,833 --> 01:01:34,100
We'll call you.

1580
01:01:34,100 --> 01:01:35,800
- You're out of sight, baby.

1581
01:01:35,800 --> 01:01:37,100
Real righteous.

1582
01:01:37,100 --> 01:01:38,167
- [Joel] What does that mean?

1583
01:01:38,167 --> 01:01:39,100
- [Crow] I don't know.

1584
01:01:39,100 --> 01:01:40,100
- Thank you, I'm flattered.

1585
01:01:40,100 --> 01:01:41,267
- [Crow] I think.

1586
01:01:41,267 --> 01:01:42,500
- Tell me something, Linda.

1587
01:01:42,500 --> 01:01:44,267
- Sure, what do
you want to know?

1588
01:01:44,267 --> 01:01:45,233
- [Servo] Does light stand still

1589
01:01:45,233 --> 01:01:47,200
on the edge of a black hole?

1590
01:01:47,200 --> 01:01:48,100
- What's your game?

1591
01:01:49,533 --> 01:01:51,733
Why do you hang around with
guys like Jeeter and Banjo for?

1592
01:01:51,733 --> 01:01:52,933
- They're the greatest.

1593
01:01:52,933 --> 01:01:55,200
With them, everything's cool.

1594
01:01:55,200 --> 01:01:56,733
Never a dull moment.

1595
01:01:56,733 --> 01:01:59,133
- [Crow] Yeah, just like
the Algonquin Round Table.

1596
01:02:01,867 --> 01:02:02,800
- What are you looking for?

1597
01:02:02,800 --> 01:02:04,467
The high living, the sports car?

1598
01:02:04,467 --> 01:02:05,933
(Linda laughs)

1599
01:02:05,933 --> 01:02:07,967
- You're not a very good
judge of character, are you?

1600
01:02:07,967 --> 01:02:08,800
- [Servo] Nope.

1601
01:02:08,800 --> 01:02:10,867
- You're square, baby.

1602
01:02:10,867 --> 01:02:12,900
So square you look like a box.

1603
01:02:12,900 --> 01:02:14,867
- [Joel] Yeah, but
there's a prize inside.

1604
01:02:14,867 --> 01:02:15,700
Ho!

1605
01:02:17,300 --> 01:02:18,400
- Well then why?

1606
01:02:18,400 --> 01:02:21,367
- The kicks, baby, the kicks.

1607
01:02:21,367 --> 01:02:22,867
- [Servo] The cereal?

1608
01:02:22,867 --> 01:02:24,667
- [Joel] Yeah, kids like
Kix for what Kix has got!

1609
01:02:24,667 --> 01:02:27,467
Moms like Kix for
what Kix is not!

1610
01:02:27,467 --> 01:02:29,533
- You're flirting with death.

1611
01:02:29,533 --> 01:02:30,700
- [Crow] Speech! Speech!

1612
01:02:30,700 --> 01:02:31,800
- You feel alive.

1613
01:02:32,967 --> 01:02:34,733
You feel like...

1614
01:02:34,733 --> 01:02:37,867
Like it's great to
be young, to be free.

1615
01:02:37,867 --> 01:02:39,433
No ring on your finger.

1616
01:02:39,433 --> 01:02:40,567
- [Servo] No bell on your toe.

1617
01:02:40,567 --> 01:02:41,900
- No snotty-nosed brats.

1618
01:02:43,100 --> 01:02:44,767
- [Joel] You make
it sound so good!

1619
01:02:44,767 --> 01:02:46,033
- Just you, alive!

1620
01:02:46,033 --> 01:02:48,033
- A bike and a robbery
aren't the same thing.

1621
01:02:48,033 --> 01:02:49,267
- [Servo] Oh, shut up, shut up!

1622
01:02:49,267 --> 01:02:51,233
- You get your kicks
from that guitar.

1623
01:02:51,233 --> 01:02:52,733
From singing.

1624
01:02:52,733 --> 01:02:54,000
- [Joel] Yeah, why?

1625
01:02:54,000 --> 01:02:54,967
- You used to get
them from having

1626
01:02:54,967 --> 01:02:56,333
400 horses in front of you

1627
01:02:56,333 --> 01:02:57,867
and death staring
you in the face.

1628
01:02:57,867 --> 01:02:59,667
- [Crow] Yeah, but that's
when he was in Ben Hur.

1629
01:02:59,667 --> 01:03:00,933
- Still not the same thing.

1630
01:03:00,933 --> 01:03:03,433
- Oh yes it is, it's the same.

1631
01:03:03,433 --> 01:03:04,900
When you look death in the face,

1632
01:03:04,900 --> 01:03:06,300
whether it's from
behind the wheel

1633
01:03:06,300 --> 01:03:07,233
or looking at a
policeman's gun...

1634
01:03:07,233 --> 01:03:08,600
- [Joel] Or in the mirror.

1635
01:03:11,133 --> 01:03:12,467
- I don't dig you.

1636
01:03:12,467 --> 01:03:13,967
- Do you dig this?

1637
01:03:13,967 --> 01:03:17,833
- [Servo] Well, I don't
know-- (muffled slurping)

1638
01:03:19,533 --> 01:03:21,033
- Are you looking for trouble?

1639
01:03:21,033 --> 01:03:22,300
- [Servo] Well you won't
find it in my dental work.

1640
01:03:22,300 --> 01:03:23,867
- Just for kicks.

1641
01:03:23,867 --> 01:03:26,767
- [Joel] Silly Rabbi,
kicks are for Trids!

1642
01:03:26,767 --> 01:03:29,767
(Servo slurping)

1643
01:03:29,767 --> 01:03:31,167
- [Crow] Is that the signal?

1644
01:03:32,833 --> 01:03:34,700
- [Servo] Well, at least
her three boyfriends

1645
01:03:34,700 --> 01:03:37,700
aren't homicidal and looking
for something like this.

1646
01:03:37,700 --> 01:03:40,467
- [Joel] You taste
like wet leaves.

1647
01:03:40,467 --> 01:03:42,433
- [Crow] Their love
can be dry cleaned.

1648
01:03:44,333 --> 01:03:46,067
- [Servo] Now what
do you mean by "mmm"?

1649
01:03:46,067 --> 01:03:47,133
- [Joel] I'd like to ask her out

1650
01:03:47,133 --> 01:03:48,733
but I'm afraid of rejection.

1651
01:03:49,767 --> 01:03:50,867
- [Crow] They're neat.

1652
01:03:52,200 --> 01:03:53,467
- [Linda] Oh...

1653
01:03:53,467 --> 01:03:55,033
- [Joel] What does "oh" mean?

1654
01:03:55,033 --> 01:03:56,000
(musical sting)

1655
01:03:56,000 --> 01:03:57,200
- [All] Huh?

1656
01:03:57,200 --> 01:03:58,033
- [Linda] Banjo!

1657
01:03:58,033 --> 01:03:59,467
- [Crow] No, Stiletto.

1658
01:04:00,967 --> 01:04:03,100
- Man, you're messing
with private stock.

1659
01:04:03,100 --> 01:04:04,867
- [Servo] Okay, now what
the hell did he say?

1660
01:04:04,867 --> 01:04:08,500
I haven't understood
a word this guy said!

1661
01:04:08,500 --> 01:04:09,333
- [Linda] No!

1662
01:04:09,333 --> 01:04:10,167
- [Crow] Uh oh.

1663
01:04:11,400 --> 01:04:13,367
- [Servo] Ooh, that had to hurt.

1664
01:04:13,367 --> 01:04:14,600
- [Joel] Banjo,

1665
01:04:14,600 --> 01:04:16,533
you're just too high strung.

1666
01:04:16,533 --> 01:04:18,033
- [Servo] Banjo
and guitar together

1667
01:04:18,033 --> 01:04:19,033
and they're dueling.

1668
01:04:21,833 --> 01:04:24,367
- [Joel] Now the guitar's gonna
beat the banjo every time.

1669
01:04:24,367 --> 01:04:25,800
- Stop him, he's gonna kill him!

1670
01:04:25,800 --> 01:04:27,400
- [Crow] Maybe
that's a good thing.

1671
01:04:35,167 --> 01:04:37,800
(Joel and bots groan)

1672
01:04:37,800 --> 01:04:39,333
- [Joel] They're rough.

1673
01:04:39,333 --> 01:04:40,900
- [Servo] Looks like Banjo's
a little out of tune there.

1674
01:04:42,133 --> 01:04:43,333
(grunts)

1675
01:04:43,333 --> 01:04:44,600
- [Joel] Yeah,
tell your friends.

1676
01:04:44,600 --> 01:04:45,433
Oh, they're here.

1677
01:04:48,033 --> 01:04:49,867
- [Crow] Eat it, boy, eat it!

1678
01:04:49,867 --> 01:04:51,133
- Hey! Cut it!

1679
01:04:51,133 --> 01:04:52,967
Then bathe in my blood.

1680
01:04:52,967 --> 01:04:54,200
- Kill him, baby!

1681
01:04:54,200 --> 01:04:55,167
Kill him!

1682
01:04:55,167 --> 01:04:56,133
Kill him off!

1683
01:04:56,133 --> 01:04:57,967
He's a loser, baby!

1684
01:04:57,967 --> 01:04:59,733
- Ah, he's not worth killing.

1685
01:04:59,733 --> 01:05:01,133
- [Servo] Not worth killing?

1686
01:05:01,133 --> 01:05:02,333
Don't you ever say that!

1687
01:05:03,400 --> 01:05:04,733
- I assume we're gettin' up

1688
01:05:06,133 --> 01:05:06,967
early tomorrow.

1689
01:05:08,467 --> 01:05:09,733
Think I'll call it a night.

1690
01:05:09,733 --> 01:05:11,233
- [Joel] Or an
afternoon or whatever.

1691
01:05:11,233 --> 01:05:12,933
I can't tell by the light.

1692
01:05:12,933 --> 01:05:15,000
(Joel laughs goofily)

1693
01:05:15,000 --> 01:05:17,200
Here's your guitar, man.

1694
01:05:17,200 --> 01:05:18,400
- [Crow] Thank you,
thank you very much.

1695
01:05:18,400 --> 01:05:20,600
I think I'm gonna go
write a song about this.

1696
01:05:25,200 --> 01:05:26,600
- What was that all about?

1697
01:05:26,600 --> 01:05:27,533
- [Servo] He kicked my butt.

1698
01:05:27,533 --> 01:05:28,533
Weren't you there?

1699
01:05:30,800 --> 01:05:31,600
- Well, baby.

1700
01:05:32,467 --> 01:05:34,067
Did you enjoy it?

1701
01:05:34,067 --> 01:05:35,333
- So you want me to vomit

1702
01:05:35,333 --> 01:05:36,600
every time another
man comes around?

1703
01:05:36,600 --> 01:05:37,733
- [Joel] Well you do
when I come around.

1704
01:05:37,733 --> 01:05:40,067
- You don't mix
business with pleasure!

1705
01:05:42,367 --> 01:05:43,967
I thought you were
supposed to be tough.

1706
01:05:43,967 --> 01:05:46,033
Next time, act it!

1707
01:05:46,033 --> 01:05:49,033
- [Servo] I hate getting notes
right after the performance.

1708
01:05:49,033 --> 01:05:51,067
- Children, we got
a busy day tomorrow.

1709
01:05:52,233 --> 01:05:53,467
Let's get some sleep.

1710
01:05:53,467 --> 01:05:55,567
- [Crow] Yeah, come
on, we got early mass.

1711
01:05:59,133 --> 01:06:00,767
Oh, the shame! The shame!

1712
01:06:01,767 --> 01:06:04,067
Oh, the pain and shame!

1713
01:06:05,400 --> 01:06:06,400
- [Joel] I'm wigging!

1714
01:06:06,400 --> 01:06:07,667
- [Servo] Whoa.

1715
01:06:07,667 --> 01:06:09,700
Meanwhile, Napoleon
Solo is in Hungary.

1716
01:06:09,700 --> 01:06:10,933
Open Channel B.

1717
01:06:12,967 --> 01:06:15,600
- [Joel] Gotta shake the dew
off the old helmet there.

1718
01:06:20,333 --> 01:06:22,700
- [Crow] Thank you, magic
night vision binoculars.

1719
01:06:22,700 --> 01:06:23,867
- [Joel] I gotta tinky.

1720
01:06:26,933 --> 01:06:28,167
- [Servo] I gotta...
(clears throat)

1721
01:06:28,167 --> 01:06:29,933
Oh, I gotta go see
a man about a horse.

1722
01:06:32,067 --> 01:06:33,533
- [Crow] (groans) What a day.

1723
01:06:34,467 --> 01:06:35,300
It's great.

1724
01:06:36,233 --> 01:06:37,167
Better lock up.

1725
01:06:37,167 --> 01:06:38,300
A lotta creeps around here.

1726
01:06:41,600 --> 01:06:43,933
- [Joel] Thanks for the
groovy charts, Mr. Squirrel,

1727
01:06:43,933 --> 01:06:45,400
wherever you are.

1728
01:06:45,400 --> 01:06:46,500
- [Servo] Heavy, guys.

1729
01:06:48,400 --> 01:06:49,633
Love their station wagon.

1730
01:06:50,933 --> 01:06:52,733
- [Crow] Okay now, everybody in?

1731
01:06:52,733 --> 01:06:53,567
Buckle up!

1732
01:06:59,267 --> 01:07:00,667
- [Joel] Hey, how
would you like someone

1733
01:07:00,667 --> 01:07:02,500
putting a cigarette out on you!

1734
01:07:02,500 --> 01:07:03,900
- [Crow] Killer spleef, man.

1735
01:07:06,333 --> 01:07:09,500
- [Joel] Figurines,
the diet crunch.

1736
