01:16:12,567 --> 01:16:14,000
- [Joel] Oh, look.

1982
01:16:14,000 --> 01:16:16,300
It's Scruffy the
lovable cop clown.

1983
01:16:17,667 --> 01:16:18,500
Jimmy hat.

1984
01:16:26,433 --> 01:16:27,367
- Okay, baby.

1985
01:16:27,367 --> 01:16:28,567
Everything's set, let's move it!

1986
01:16:28,567 --> 01:16:30,033
- [Servo] He must be psychic.

1987
01:16:32,000 --> 01:16:32,933
- [Linda] The guard's
out of the way.

1988
01:16:32,933 --> 01:16:33,867
- [Crow] What do you mean?

1989
01:16:33,867 --> 01:16:34,867
He's in the middle of the floor!

1990
01:16:34,867 --> 01:16:36,867
- Move! I said move!

1991
01:16:36,867 --> 01:16:38,267
Fats, fill them bags!

1992
01:16:38,267 --> 01:16:39,500
You, blondie, over here!

1993
01:16:39,500 --> 01:16:41,667
- [Servo] What is he
speaking in Sanskrit?

1994
01:16:41,667 --> 01:16:42,867
Slow down!

1995
01:16:42,867 --> 01:16:44,067
- Fats, you and Linda
go get the money!

1996
01:16:44,067 --> 01:16:45,533
- [Crow] It's code.

1997
01:16:45,533 --> 01:16:47,733
- [Joel] I want firm tummies
and a nice straight dance line.

1998
01:16:47,733 --> 01:16:48,567
Come on!

1999
01:16:51,100 --> 01:16:52,333
- [Crow] Oh, great.

2000
01:16:52,333 --> 01:16:53,433
There's stamps and
some paperclips

2001
01:16:53,433 --> 01:16:54,967
and Garfield sticker and hey,

2002
01:16:54,967 --> 01:16:57,000
grab that statue that says
World's Greatest Grandma!

2003
01:16:57,000 --> 01:16:58,633
- [Servo] Hey look, ten dollars!

2004
01:16:58,633 --> 01:16:59,900
We're set for the
rest of our lives

2005
01:16:59,900 --> 01:17:02,200
unless we wanna buy a
12-pack or somethin'.

2006
01:17:02,200 --> 01:17:04,633
- [Crow] Hey, they play
the Ventures at this bank.

2007
01:17:05,500 --> 01:17:06,900
- [Joel] They got everything.

2008
01:17:06,900 --> 01:17:08,533
Stadium blanket, calendar,
Lincoln coin bank!

2009
01:17:10,167 --> 01:17:11,667
- [Servo] Look at the bank sign.

2010
01:17:11,667 --> 01:17:14,367
It's printed with electrician's
tape on ceiling tile.

2011
01:17:14,367 --> 01:17:16,867
- [Crow] Thinking of growing
a Van Dyke, what do ya think?

2012
01:17:18,067 --> 01:17:20,067
- [Joel] Did you see
Cop Rock last night?

2013
01:17:20,067 --> 01:17:20,900
It sucked.

2014
01:17:23,567 --> 01:17:24,900
- [Servo] Hmm...

2015
01:17:26,333 --> 01:17:28,600
Now, if I could just remember
by Aldis code from the Navy.

2016
01:17:28,600 --> 01:17:29,667
- Look at the lights!

2017
01:17:31,300 --> 01:17:32,800
- [Servo] What about 'em?

2018
01:17:32,800 --> 01:17:33,800
- [Joel] Whoa.

2019
01:17:33,800 --> 01:17:35,033
You're bright!

2020
01:17:35,033 --> 01:17:36,433
- [Servo] Hey, man,
he's doin' Aldis code!

2021
01:17:39,400 --> 01:17:42,233
(all whispering "help")

2022
01:17:42,233 --> 01:17:43,500
- Looks like he's
trying to signal us.

2023
01:17:43,500 --> 01:17:45,433
- [Joel] Oh, no, he's
just testin' his lights.

2024
01:17:45,433 --> 01:17:47,567
Let's go dunk a couple
of spud nuts, eh, Phil?

2025
01:17:47,567 --> 01:17:48,900
(rapid tapping)

2026
01:17:48,900 --> 01:17:50,367
- [Crow] Hey, is that their car?

2027
01:17:50,367 --> 01:17:52,300
Sounds like they
got a tappet loose.

2028
01:17:54,000 --> 01:17:55,433
(muffled tapping)

2029
01:17:55,433 --> 01:17:56,267
That's better.

2030
01:17:58,300 --> 01:17:59,900
- [Servo] What's all this then?

2031
01:17:59,900 --> 01:18:01,800
I mean, what's
goin' on here, boy?

2032
01:18:05,233 --> 01:18:07,400
- Well, son, what's
the lights for?

2033
01:18:07,400 --> 01:18:09,100
- [Joel] Illuminating
the road after dark, sir?

2034
01:18:09,100 --> 01:18:10,267
- There's three men and
a girl robbin' that bank.

2035
01:18:10,267 --> 01:18:11,300
- [All] And a baby.

2036
01:18:12,700 --> 01:18:14,233
- Jeeter!

2037
01:18:14,233 --> 01:18:15,167
It's the Gestapo and they're
talkin' to Rod, let's split!

2038
01:18:15,167 --> 01:18:16,800
- [Crow] No, you're the Gestapo.

2039
01:18:16,800 --> 01:18:17,733
- Linda, Fats!

2040
01:18:17,733 --> 01:18:19,000
Grab that loot, let's go!

2041
01:18:19,000 --> 01:18:20,500
- This better not be a joke.

2042
01:18:20,500 --> 01:18:21,700
- [Servo] Well, it is a
joke, but it's still true.

2043
01:18:21,700 --> 01:18:23,033
- Stay put, kid.

2044
01:18:25,333 --> 01:18:27,100
- [Servo] Here we go.

2045
01:18:28,367 --> 01:18:29,867
- [Joel] That's a
nice wide spread.

2046
01:18:29,867 --> 01:18:31,700
He must have had a
modified choke on that.

2047
01:18:31,700 --> 01:18:33,400
- Banjo just hit a
couple of the fuzz!

2048
01:18:33,400 --> 01:18:34,467
- [All] What?

2049
01:18:39,633 --> 01:18:40,567
- Hold it, creep!

2050
01:18:40,567 --> 01:18:41,900
Or I'll blow your brains out!

2051
01:18:41,900 --> 01:18:44,267
- Come on, move!

2052
01:18:44,267 --> 01:18:45,700
Linda, hurry up!

2053
01:18:45,700 --> 01:18:47,800
- [Crow] In these
heels? Are you crazy?

2054
01:18:51,533 --> 01:18:53,133
- [Joel] Okay, comin' boss.

2055
01:18:53,133 --> 01:18:54,633
- [Crow] Nice tag.

2056
01:18:56,233 --> 01:18:57,400
(bell rings)

2057
01:18:57,400 --> 01:18:59,033
- [Servo] School's
out! Recess, everybody!

2058
01:19:04,033 --> 01:19:06,300
- [Crow] Okay, now we all
saw the Zupruder film.

2059
01:19:06,300 --> 01:19:08,167
You be Kennedy! (laughs)

2060
01:19:08,167 --> 01:19:09,400
- [Banjo] He signaled the man!

2061
01:19:09,400 --> 01:19:10,200
- [Jeeter] Banjo,
get in the car.

2062
01:19:10,200 --> 01:19:11,400
Banjo, get in the car!

2063
01:19:11,400 --> 01:19:12,233
- [All] What?

2064
01:19:13,667 --> 01:19:15,833
- That wasn't a very
nice thing to do.

2065
01:19:15,833 --> 01:19:16,900
- If Banjo's telling the truth,

2066
01:19:16,900 --> 01:19:18,633
why don't we just dump him now?

2067
01:19:18,633 --> 01:19:21,267
- Because this creep is gonna
get us away from little men.

2068
01:19:21,267 --> 01:19:23,333
He's gonna drive the
race of his life.

2069
01:19:23,333 --> 01:19:24,967
Put your foot to
the floorboard, man.

2070
01:19:24,967 --> 01:19:25,900
Move it!

2071
01:19:25,900 --> 01:19:27,033
I said move it!

2072
01:19:27,033 --> 01:19:28,033
- [Joel] But remember
your seatbelt.

2073
01:19:28,033 --> 01:19:29,300
Check your blind spot.

2074
01:19:29,300 --> 01:19:30,767
Three point check!
That's better.

2075
01:19:30,767 --> 01:19:31,967
- [Servo] No, not this way, man!

2076
01:19:31,967 --> 01:19:33,400
My mom will see me! Oh!

2077
01:19:35,833 --> 01:19:37,100
- [Jeeter] Come on,
man, earn your money!

2078
01:19:37,100 --> 01:19:38,133
Faster! Faster!

2079
01:19:43,233 --> 01:19:45,067
- [Crow] Oh, you poor officer!

2080
01:19:45,067 --> 01:19:46,267
Can I get you a donut?

2081
01:19:47,833 --> 01:19:49,800
- [Joel] (grunting)
Your knee on my chest!

2082
01:19:51,333 --> 01:19:53,133
- [Servo] I'm sorry
but you're dead.

2083
01:19:54,067 --> 01:19:54,900
No donuts.

2084
01:19:57,233 --> 01:19:58,133
- [Joel] Poor guy.

2085
01:20:00,033 --> 01:20:01,300
- Mayday, mayday.

2086
01:20:01,300 --> 01:20:03,433
- [Crow] He used to be a pilot.

2087
01:20:03,433 --> 01:20:05,467
- [Servo] I used too much rouge!

2088
01:20:05,467 --> 01:20:07,367
- ...just robbed the
Citrusville bank.

2089
01:20:08,267 --> 01:20:09,933
- 5-O-7 to all units.

2090
01:20:09,933 --> 01:20:12,000
5-O-7 to all units.

2091
01:20:12,000 --> 01:20:13,400
Whatever your location,

2092
01:20:13,400 --> 01:20:15,900
proceed to roadblock
stations around Citrusville.

2093
01:20:15,900 --> 01:20:17,400
- [Joel] Uh, we are
all the units, sir.

2094
01:20:17,400 --> 01:20:20,667
- ...proceed to roadblock
stations around Citrusville.

2095
01:20:20,667 --> 01:20:22,500
- [Crow] Ha! They're gonna
put the squeeze on 'em in

2096
01:20:22,500 --> 01:20:23,900
Citrusville! (laughs)

2097
01:20:23,900 --> 01:20:26,000
- [Servo] Nelson Riddle
and his orchestra!

2098
01:20:27,467 --> 01:20:28,467
- [Crow] Squeeze on
'em, see, 'cause--

2099
01:20:28,467 --> 01:20:30,533
- [Servo] Yeah, we got it, Crow.

2100
01:20:30,533 --> 01:20:32,733
- [Crow] What's Citrusville
famous for, you suppose?

2101
01:20:32,733 --> 01:20:33,700
- [Servo] Probably
dairy products.

2102
01:20:33,700 --> 01:20:34,600
- [Crow] I... huh?

2103
01:20:35,800 --> 01:20:37,800
- [Joel] Police cars
courtesy of Grandma.

2104
01:20:41,467 --> 01:20:43,133
- [Jeeter] You're
doing great, baby.

2105
01:20:43,133 --> 01:20:44,400
- [Crow] Don't call
me that at work.

2106
01:20:44,400 --> 01:20:45,767
- Hey, that looks
like their car!

2107
01:20:45,767 --> 01:20:46,733
- [Servo] Naw!

2108
01:20:46,733 --> 01:20:48,067
Couldn't be, they're miles away.

2109
01:20:48,067 --> 01:20:49,567
(gunshots fire)

2110
01:20:49,567 --> 01:20:52,033
(Banjo yells)

2111
01:20:54,000 --> 01:20:55,367
- [Servo] That'll teach him.

2112
01:21:01,067 --> 01:21:02,867
- [Crow] Calgon, take me away!

2113
01:21:04,900 --> 01:21:07,700
- [Joel] I got one
in my hair! Crawlers!

2114
01:21:07,700 --> 01:21:08,967
- [Servo] Stupid old bun!

2115
01:21:10,200 --> 01:21:11,400
- Another one for me.

2116
01:21:11,400 --> 01:21:13,433
- [Joel] You know, this
really is kinda fun!

2117
01:21:17,767 --> 01:21:19,367
I'm having a really good time!

2118
01:21:21,267 --> 01:21:23,533
- [Crow] I'll get a
Kleenex, Bob. Stay there.

2119
01:21:25,467 --> 01:21:26,900
- [Servo] Officer
down, officer down.

2120
01:21:26,900 --> 01:21:28,100
I need bear claws...

2121
01:21:28,100 --> 01:21:29,733
I mean, backup, send
a jelly donut...

2122
01:21:29,733 --> 01:21:31,400
I mean, send help.

2123
01:21:31,400 --> 01:21:34,167
- [Cop] Gang headed
east on Old Citrus Road.

2124
01:21:34,167 --> 01:21:35,367
Just killed my partner.

2125
01:21:35,367 --> 01:21:37,400
- [Joel] And I'm all
busted up inside, over.

2126
01:21:38,833 --> 01:21:40,300
- [Banjo] Here comes the fuzz!

2127
01:21:40,300 --> 01:21:41,967
- [All] Here comes the
fuzz! Here comes the fuzz!

2128
01:21:41,967 --> 01:21:43,833
Fuzz is comin'!

2129
01:21:43,833 --> 01:21:45,633
(siren blares)

2130
01:21:45,633 --> 01:21:47,033
- [Servo] He's
doing really well.

2131
01:21:47,033 --> 01:21:48,400
- [Crow] Yeah, this is
the longest he's driven

2132
01:21:48,400 --> 01:21:50,567
without rolling and burning.

2133
01:21:50,567 --> 01:21:52,467
- [Banjo] Another roadblock!

2134
01:21:52,467 --> 01:21:55,500
- [Jeeter] Drive through
it, man, drive through it!

2135
01:21:55,500 --> 01:21:56,300
- [Servo] Whoa!

2136
01:21:57,733 --> 01:21:58,967
- [Joel] You know, we
really should have blocked

2137
01:21:58,967 --> 01:21:59,900
the other road, too.

2138
01:21:59,900 --> 01:22:01,300
What were we thinking?

2139
01:22:01,300 --> 01:22:02,600
- [Crow] Roadblock detour.

2140
01:22:03,700 --> 01:22:05,200
- [Banjo] Down the
Yellow Brick Road, man!

2141
01:22:05,200 --> 01:22:08,367
- [Servo] Guess we're not
in Kansas anymore, dude!

2142
01:22:08,367 --> 01:22:09,333
Go kill Dorothy.

2143
01:22:10,767 --> 01:22:11,900
- [Crow] That's kind of
like closing the barn door

2144
01:22:11,900 --> 01:22:12,967
after the cows are out.

2145
01:22:12,967 --> 01:22:14,667
Come on, dummy.

2146
01:22:14,667 --> 01:22:16,967
- [Joel] Signal
your turn, please.

2147
01:22:16,967 --> 01:22:17,800
Oh well.

2148
01:22:21,400 --> 01:22:23,133
- [Crow] What's he gonna
do, shoot at oranges?

2149
01:22:23,133 --> 01:22:24,200
- [Servo] Looks like it.

2150
01:22:24,200 --> 01:22:26,767
(gunshots fire)
(siren blares)

2151
01:22:26,767 --> 01:22:28,233
(tires screech)

2152
01:22:28,233 --> 01:22:30,100
- [Servo] Oh, now, that's
a fire siren. Come on!

2153
01:22:31,800 --> 01:22:34,467
(gunshot fires)

2154
01:22:36,500 --> 01:22:38,067
- [Joel] I'm huge! I'm immense!

2155
01:22:39,567 --> 01:22:41,233
- [Crow] Hey,
look, Erik Estrada!

2156
01:22:43,000 --> 01:22:44,267
- [Jeeter] Slow 'em down, Banjo!

2157
01:22:45,200 --> 01:22:47,367
(gunshot fires)

2158
01:22:47,367 --> 01:22:49,100
Two barrels for
Banjo, comin' up!

2159
01:22:49,100 --> 01:22:51,033
- [Servo] Did he say
"two bowels for Banjo"?

2160
01:22:51,033 --> 01:22:52,400
- [Joel] Bedtime for Banjo?

2161
01:22:53,567 --> 01:22:54,400
- [Crow] Would you
get your arms and legs

2162
01:22:54,400 --> 01:22:55,400
inside this car, please?

2163
01:22:57,033 --> 01:22:59,067
- [Joel] How am I
doin' it? I don't know!

2164
01:23:00,467 --> 01:23:01,700
- [Banjo] Man, we rollin'!

2165
01:23:01,700 --> 01:23:03,033
- [Joel] You wanna
get some waggits

2166
01:23:03,033 --> 01:23:04,033
and some rolls

2167
01:23:04,033 --> 01:23:05,267
and some reezen-rozzen.

2168
01:23:05,267 --> 01:23:06,933
(Servo laughs gravelly)

2169
01:23:06,933 --> 01:23:08,267
Everyday!

2170
01:23:08,267 --> 01:23:09,567
All along the way.

2171
01:23:10,633 --> 01:23:11,567
- [Crow] By this time,

2172
01:23:11,567 --> 01:23:12,533
the old Duke boys had killed

2173
01:23:12,533 --> 01:23:14,800
just about every cop in town.

2174
01:23:14,800 --> 01:23:17,367
And Daisy had slipped into
somethin' more comfortable.

2175
01:23:17,367 --> 01:23:18,633
(tires screech)

2176
01:23:18,633 --> 01:23:19,900
- [Servo] Oh, it's
a squealing swamp.

2177
01:23:19,900 --> 01:23:22,267
Oh, there's the exploding bush.

2178
01:23:22,267 --> 01:23:23,733
- [Jeeter] Earn your money!

2179
01:23:23,733 --> 01:23:25,667
Drive, baby, drive!

2180
01:23:25,667 --> 01:23:27,133
- [Crow] What do you
think I'm doing?!

2181
01:23:27,133 --> 01:23:29,300
Oh, look, I'm cranky
and hungry, I'm sorry.

2182
01:23:31,233 --> 01:23:33,267
- [Joel] Back into
the squealing swamp.

2183
01:23:33,267 --> 01:23:34,633
- [Servo] So this is the
point where the director said,

2184
01:23:34,633 --> 01:23:36,533
"Use everything we shot."

2185
01:23:36,533 --> 01:23:37,367
- What's wrong with the car?

2186
01:23:37,367 --> 01:23:38,300
- [Joel] Who's talking?

2187
01:23:38,300 --> 01:23:39,100
- They musta hit the gas tank.

2188
01:23:39,100 --> 01:23:40,267
- [Joel] Who's talking?

2189
01:23:40,267 --> 01:23:41,433
- [Servo] I dunno.

2190
01:23:41,433 --> 01:23:42,700
- [Jeeter] See the
lighthouse? Stop there.

2191
01:23:42,700 --> 01:23:44,033
- [Servo] Lighthouse?
They're in the woods!

2192
01:23:44,033 --> 01:23:45,933
- [Crow] Going down.
We've lost an engine.

2193
01:23:45,933 --> 01:23:47,467
(siren blares)
(gunshot fires)

2194
01:23:47,467 --> 01:23:48,500
- [Servo] Lighthouse?

2195
01:23:50,267 --> 01:23:51,567
- [Joel] Oh, it's
for Winnebagos.

2196
01:23:52,767 --> 01:23:53,700
- [Crow] Well, it's
up to the Navy now.

2197
01:23:53,700 --> 01:23:55,967
It's out of our jurisdiction.

2198
01:23:55,967 --> 01:23:56,967
- Come on baby, let's go!

2199
01:23:56,967 --> 01:23:58,433
- [Joel] Whoa! That's too close.

2200
01:24:00,200 --> 01:24:01,433
Stop calling me baby.

2201
01:24:05,400 --> 01:24:06,733
- [Crow] Oh, great hideout.

2202
01:24:06,733 --> 01:24:08,000
If they have to
spend any time there,

2203
01:24:08,000 --> 01:24:09,833
they can eat the
bricks, I guess.

2204
01:24:09,833 --> 01:24:11,767
- [Joel] Oh, look, they're
in a nautilus, you guys.

2205
01:24:11,767 --> 01:24:13,400
- [Servo] It's like
the Time Tunnel.

2206
01:24:18,900 --> 01:24:20,933
- [Crow] Don't shoot
the car, we need that!

2207
01:24:22,700 --> 01:24:23,633
- [Servo] Oh, sorry!

2208
01:24:23,633 --> 01:24:25,400
Accidentally shot a cop, sorry.

2209
01:24:25,400 --> 01:24:26,600
- [Jeeter] Load it up, Linda.

2210
01:24:26,600 --> 01:24:27,900
It's just like shooting
ducks in an alley.

2211
01:24:27,900 --> 01:24:29,167
- [Joel] I think it's
fish in a barrel,

2212
01:24:29,167 --> 01:24:30,433
but I know what you mean,

2213
01:24:30,433 --> 01:24:32,167
and you'll know what
we mean after this.

2214
01:24:44,167 --> 01:24:46,400
- [Servo] For the glory
of the SLA, Tanya.

2215
01:24:46,400 --> 01:24:50,067
- [Joel] I just got a thing
about girls with guns, I dunno.

2216
01:24:50,067 --> 01:24:52,367
(gunshots fire)

2217
01:24:52,367 --> 01:24:53,833
- [Servo] Hi.

2218
01:24:53,833 --> 01:24:54,900
- [Crow] Here you go, Hoss.

2219
01:24:54,900 --> 01:24:56,200
Nice shootin', Little Joe!

2220
01:25:00,200 --> 01:25:00,967
My hair's stuck!

2221
01:25:02,067 --> 01:25:03,400
- [Joel] I'm old enough
to drive and drink

2222
01:25:03,400 --> 01:25:05,000
but not be in a war.

2223
01:25:05,000 --> 01:25:06,933
What do you think?

2224
01:25:06,933 --> 01:25:08,633
- [Servo] Hey, it's Diana Rigg.

2225
01:25:10,200 --> 01:25:11,200
- [Crow] Join us!

2226
01:25:12,333 --> 01:25:14,400
- [Servo] Gettin'
enough kicks now, baby?

2227
01:25:17,100 --> 01:25:17,933
Yeah.

2228
01:25:20,100 --> 01:25:23,367
Look, you got somethin'
to say, say it.

2229
01:25:26,467 --> 01:25:29,300
- [Joel] You killed
a tree, Banjo!

2230
01:25:31,600 --> 01:25:32,500
- [Crow] Oh, oh-oh, oh-oh!

2231
01:25:32,500 --> 01:25:33,767
Excuse me!

2232
01:25:33,767 --> 01:25:35,033
- [Banjo] I got me one!

2233
01:25:35,033 --> 01:25:36,267
I got me a man!

2234
01:25:36,267 --> 01:25:38,400
- [Servo] I'm happy for
ya, now go shoot cops.

2235
01:25:41,300 --> 01:25:42,700
- [Joel] Quite a dance move.

2236
01:25:46,100 --> 01:25:47,800
- [Servo] Oh! My head's
tryin' to blow up!

2237
01:25:47,800 --> 01:25:50,067
- I can't make it here,
man! I can't make it!

2238
01:25:50,067 --> 01:25:52,667
- [Joel] He's wigging!

2239
01:25:52,667 --> 01:25:54,300
Banjo, don't be a hero!

2240
01:25:55,567 --> 01:25:58,067
- [Servo] Come back, Banjo!

2241
01:25:58,067 --> 01:26:00,133
Stupid old gun!

2242
01:26:00,133 --> 01:26:02,500
- Cover him, Fats, cover him!

2243
01:26:04,600 --> 01:26:05,833
- [Servo] Now, wait a minute.

2244
01:26:05,833 --> 01:26:08,000
Banjo's about two feet
away, look at that.

2245
01:26:08,000 --> 01:26:09,433
Two feet away from the cops.

2246
01:26:10,633 --> 01:26:11,467
Criminy.

2247
01:26:14,933 --> 01:26:17,500
- [Joel] He's over there, yeah.

2248
01:26:20,800 --> 01:26:22,133
- [Servo] Uh oh.

2249
01:26:23,533 --> 01:26:25,133
- [Joel] That's pretty good
with a shotgun at that distance.

2250
01:26:25,133 --> 01:26:26,933
- [Crow] Must be
using a full choke.

2251
01:26:30,833 --> 01:26:32,033
- The lousy men got him.

2252
01:26:32,033 --> 01:26:34,000
They got Banjo!

2253
01:26:34,000 --> 01:26:36,000
- [Joel] They torched
his bike, too.

2254
01:26:36,000 --> 01:26:36,933
- Grab the rifle.

2255
01:26:36,933 --> 01:26:38,433
Go upstairs as fast as you can.

2256
01:26:38,433 --> 01:26:39,367
See if you can pick off
any of them from upstairs.

2257
01:26:39,367 --> 01:26:40,867
- [Crow] O-thay.

2258
01:26:40,867 --> 01:26:43,067
I'll be running up there now.

2259
01:26:43,067 --> 01:26:45,633
(Crow panting)

2260
01:26:50,700 --> 01:26:53,267
(Crow panting)

2261
01:26:58,633 --> 01:27:00,533
(Crow panting)

2262
01:27:00,533 --> 01:27:01,600
- [Servo] Long way up.

2263
01:27:06,267 --> 01:27:08,833
(Crow panting)

2264
01:27:11,733 --> 01:27:13,400
- [Servo] Oh! They
got my foot, Charlie!

2265
01:27:13,400 --> 01:27:14,633
They got my foot.

2266
01:27:14,633 --> 01:27:16,333
- [Crow] Hey, it's
a double helix.

2267
01:27:17,767 --> 01:27:19,400
- [Servo] Thank you for
the Crick and Watson joke.

2268
01:27:20,967 --> 01:27:22,700
- [Joel] You know, he's
kind of an easy target.

2269
01:27:22,700 --> 01:27:24,767
Fat, drunk and
stupid, I wonder...

2270
01:27:26,567 --> 01:27:28,467
- [Crow] He could
never hit him though.

2271
01:27:28,467 --> 01:27:30,900
- [Servo] One if by
land, two if by stupid.

2272
01:27:33,400 --> 01:27:36,133
(dramatic music)

2273
01:27:37,533 --> 01:27:39,467
- [Crow] Hey, I've always
wanted that cool lid.

2274
01:27:39,467 --> 01:27:41,533
- [Servo] Philip Glass music!

2275
01:27:41,533 --> 01:27:44,033
- [Joel] I always thought
only the good died young.

2276
01:27:44,033 --> 01:27:45,200
- [Servo] Live fast, die young,

2277
01:27:45,200 --> 01:27:47,067
and leave a fat,
bloated, ugly corpse.

2278
01:27:48,967 --> 01:27:51,633
(gunshots fire)

2279
01:27:54,433 --> 01:27:55,633
Here we go again with him.

2280
01:27:55,633 --> 01:27:56,900
- [Crow] Uh oh.

2281
01:27:56,900 --> 01:27:57,833
- Fats!

2282
01:27:57,833 --> 01:27:58,667
Fats, he's comin' your way!

2283
01:27:58,667 --> 01:28:00,300
Kill him! Kill him!

2284
01:28:01,133 --> 01:28:02,600
Hand me the shotgun!

2285
01:28:02,600 --> 01:28:03,533
- [Servo] Quick.

2286
01:28:03,533 --> 01:28:06,700
(Servo panting)

2287
01:28:06,700 --> 01:28:08,667
- [Crow] Oh, I
gotta quit smokin'.

2288
01:28:08,667 --> 01:28:10,900
(Servo panting)

2289
01:28:10,900 --> 01:28:12,000
(jazzy beat)

2290
01:28:12,000 --> 01:28:14,500
(Servo scats)

2291
01:28:22,467 --> 01:28:23,400
- [Servo] Now,
now wait a minute!

2292
01:28:23,400 --> 01:28:24,967
Just, just wait a minute here!

2293
01:28:25,900 --> 01:28:27,200
- [Joel] I will kill you!

2294
01:28:33,067 --> 01:28:34,300
- [Crow] I'm gettin' dizzy.

2295
01:28:34,300 --> 01:28:35,133
- [Servo] Me too.

2296
01:28:39,367 --> 01:28:40,633
(gunshot fires)

2297
01:28:40,633 --> 01:28:42,433
- [Joel] Hey, that's
not completely fair!

2298
01:28:45,300 --> 01:28:46,933
- [Crow] Hey, mister,
can you help me?

2299
01:28:46,933 --> 01:28:48,167
I need so--

2300
01:28:48,167 --> 01:28:49,100
- [Servo] You know in
a more expensive movie,

2301
01:28:49,100 --> 01:28:50,567
they would have tossed him over.

2302
01:28:50,567 --> 01:28:53,767
- [Joel] Or at least used
him as a shield or something.

2303
01:28:53,767 --> 01:28:54,967
- [Crow] It's filled with Pez!

2304
01:29:01,100 --> 01:29:01,900
- [Servo] He's upstairs.

2305
01:29:01,900 --> 01:29:02,833
Thanks, Fats.

2306
01:29:02,833 --> 01:29:04,133
You know, you're smarter dead.

2307
01:29:07,967 --> 01:29:10,467
Sounds like Johnny Cash music.

2308
01:29:11,967 --> 01:29:13,200
- [Crow] Kill, kill, kill.

2309
01:29:13,200 --> 01:29:14,233
Die, die, die!

2310
01:29:14,233 --> 01:29:15,100
When will it end?!

2311
01:29:15,100 --> 01:29:16,367
- [Servo] I dunno.

2312
01:29:17,867 --> 01:29:19,600
- [Joel] Oh, man, you
got my windbreaker!

2313
01:29:19,600 --> 01:29:22,067
This is a Members Only,
too, it's not cheap!

2314
01:29:22,067 --> 01:29:23,833
Oh, I'm no good at
anything, I'm terrible.

2315
01:29:23,833 --> 01:29:25,567
I can't drive, can't shoot.

2316
01:29:25,567 --> 01:29:27,433
What the hell am I good at?!

2317
01:29:28,600 --> 01:29:30,533
Oh, jeepers, I'll never
get in another movie.

2318
01:29:33,733 --> 01:29:35,267
- [Servo] At least
the music's gone.

2319
01:29:35,267 --> 01:29:36,100
Ow!

2320
01:29:36,100 --> 01:29:37,700
- Well if it isn't Rod.

2321
01:29:37,700 --> 01:29:38,533
- [Servo] What?

2322
01:29:41,267 --> 01:29:42,467
- [Crow] Uh oh.

2323
01:29:42,467 --> 01:29:43,400
- [Servo] Yeah, he's
gettin' serious.

2324
01:29:43,400 --> 01:29:45,100
He took his sunglasses off.

2325
01:29:45,100 --> 01:29:46,033
Whoa!

2326
01:29:46,033 --> 01:29:46,833
- [Crow] Servo, save yourself!

2327
01:29:46,833 --> 01:29:48,333
Get outta the way!

2328
01:29:48,333 --> 01:29:51,133
(Jeeter laughs)

2329
01:29:51,133 --> 01:29:52,133
- See ya later.

2330
01:29:52,133 --> 01:29:53,100
- [Servo] Alligator.

2331
01:29:53,100 --> 01:29:54,133
Not!

2332
01:29:54,133 --> 01:29:56,633
(gunshot fires)

2333
01:29:56,633 --> 01:29:58,300
- [Joel] What gives?

2334
01:29:58,300 --> 01:29:59,900
(Jeeter screams)

2335
01:29:59,900 --> 01:30:01,900
Oh, he's all bendy
and floppy and stuff.

2336
01:30:02,867 --> 01:30:04,100
- [Crow] That was kinda neat.

2337
01:30:04,100 --> 01:30:06,200
(Servo laughs)

2338
01:30:06,200 --> 01:30:07,567
- [Servo] Sorry.

2339
01:30:07,567 --> 01:30:09,100
- [Joel] Heavy.

2340
01:30:09,100 --> 01:30:10,533
- [Servo] It kinda looks like
the beginning of a Bond film,

2341
01:30:10,533 --> 01:30:12,133
doesn't it?

2342
01:30:12,133 --> 01:30:15,300
- [Crow] Hey, there's the girl
with the golden gun! (laughs)

2343
01:30:16,533 --> 01:30:19,867
(Servo sighs)

2344
01:30:19,867 --> 01:30:21,333
- [Joel] It's been a big day.

2345
01:30:21,333 --> 01:30:23,633
- [Servo] I'm just not
havin' a good week.

2346
01:30:29,300 --> 01:30:30,700
Here.

2347
01:30:30,700 --> 01:30:31,567
A gift for you.

2348
01:30:33,100 --> 01:30:34,833
- [Crow] I didn't
get you anything.

2349
01:30:38,233 --> 01:30:40,067
- Kicks, baby.

2350
01:30:40,067 --> 01:30:41,500
- [Joel] They're not for Trids.

2351
01:30:41,500 --> 01:30:42,300
- Kicks.

2352
01:30:44,200 --> 01:30:46,233
It was the wildest.

2353
01:30:46,233 --> 01:30:48,667
- [Servo] Kicks just keep
getting harder to find.

2354
01:30:48,667 --> 01:30:49,900
- [Crow] Ew!

2355
01:30:49,900 --> 01:30:52,000
You still taste like
Fatty, don't you brush?

2356
01:30:55,667 --> 01:30:56,967
- [Servo] Oh, she's crying.

2357
01:31:01,700 --> 01:31:04,133
- Charlie, go on
up and check Fats.

2358
01:31:04,133 --> 01:31:05,333
Take her away, Bob.

2359
01:31:05,333 --> 01:31:07,267
- [Servo] Are there
kicks in prison, honey?

2360
01:31:12,333 --> 01:31:13,500
- [Joel] I'm here, Bob.

2361
01:31:15,167 --> 01:31:16,600
♪ I know ♪

2362
01:31:16,600 --> 01:31:18,067
- [Servo] Here we go again.

2363
01:31:18,067 --> 01:31:19,333
♪ All your ways ♪

2364
01:31:19,333 --> 01:31:20,800
- [Joel] You know,
I love that song.

2365
01:31:20,800 --> 01:31:23,800
And I like your
Ralston-Purina suit, too.

2366
01:31:25,200 --> 01:31:26,533
- [Crow] Check.

2367
01:31:26,533 --> 01:31:28,100
Hey! It's God-cam.

2368
01:31:28,100 --> 01:31:30,800
♪ I like ♪

2369
01:31:30,800 --> 01:31:34,433
♪ What I know ♪

2370
01:31:34,433 --> 01:31:36,133
♪ About you ♪

2371
01:31:36,133 --> 01:31:36,967
- [Joel] I see.

2372
01:31:39,833 --> 01:31:42,700
(Servo swoons)

2373
01:31:42,700 --> 01:31:43,933
- [Joel] You know,

2374
01:31:43,933 --> 01:31:46,733
I'm gonna miss her and
all her murderous ways.

2375
01:31:49,133 --> 01:31:50,200
- [Crow] She was neat.

2376
01:31:51,333 --> 01:31:52,900
- [Servo] In a sick sort of way.

2377
01:31:55,700 --> 01:31:57,533
Well, Rod, 13 dead cops,

2378
01:31:57,533 --> 01:31:59,067
six dead innocent bystanders,

2379
01:31:59,067 --> 01:32:00,167
a couple of dead bikers.

2380
01:32:00,167 --> 01:32:01,433
Good work!

2381
01:32:01,433 --> 01:32:02,233
I'd like to have you on
my team again sometime.

2382
01:32:02,233 --> 01:32:03,533
What do you think?

2383
01:32:05,900 --> 01:32:07,400
- [Joel] Signal the God-cam.

2384
01:32:08,567 --> 01:32:09,833
- [Crow] 'Cause I
get a kick outta...

2385
01:32:09,833 --> 01:32:12,667
Oh, wrong song, sorry. (laughs)

2386
01:32:12,667 --> 01:32:14,167
- [Servo] Louie,

2387
01:32:14,167 --> 01:32:16,167
this could be the start
of a beautiful friendship.

2388
01:32:18,533 --> 01:32:20,200
- [Joel] Man, when you
were trying to signal me,

2389
01:32:20,200 --> 01:32:21,467
that was so funny.

2390
01:32:21,467 --> 01:32:23,200
I thought you were
kissing the girl.

2391
01:32:23,200 --> 01:32:25,300
I thought that was
the sign... oh, boy.

2392
01:32:25,300 --> 01:32:27,533
Well we can laugh
about it now but...

2393
01:32:27,533 --> 01:32:28,767
Whatcha doin' now?

2394
01:32:30,700 --> 01:32:32,033
- [Crow] Do you live alone?

2395
01:32:33,200 --> 01:32:34,867
Would you like to?

2396
01:32:34,867 --> 01:32:36,933
- [Servo] I've had enough.
Let's get outta here.

2397
01:32:36,933 --> 01:32:38,333
- [Joel] We should really go.

2398
01:32:38,333 --> 01:32:39,800
Come on.

2399
01:32:39,800 --> 01:32:41,600
(grunting) You're getting
heavy, you know that?

2400
01:32:56,067 --> 01:32:59,500
You know, guys, I feel
great, I'm flyin' high!

2401
01:32:59,500 --> 01:33:00,800
- Huh?

2402
01:33:00,800 --> 01:33:02,067
- Joel, how can you feel good

2403
01:33:02,067 --> 01:33:04,333
after that kidney
stone of a movie?

2404
01:33:05,233 --> 01:33:06,633
- Yeah, I'm downright depressed.

2405
01:33:06,633 --> 01:33:09,767
If I had wrists, I'd contemplate
slitting them right now.

2406
01:33:09,767 --> 01:33:10,700
- What, huh?

2407
01:33:10,700 --> 01:33:12,200
- This movie!

2408
01:33:12,200 --> 01:33:14,133
It was like spending the
weekend with your dentist!

2409
01:33:15,067 --> 01:33:16,600
- Oh you guys, listen.

2410
01:33:16,600 --> 01:33:18,533
You gotta take it easier,
it's just a movie.

2411
01:33:18,533 --> 01:33:22,833
Yes, it was like being pulled
through a dark, tarry abyss,

2412
01:33:22,833 --> 01:33:23,767
but it's only a movie.

2413
01:33:23,767 --> 01:33:24,933
You gotta use your intelligence

2414
01:33:24,933 --> 01:33:26,767
to abstract yourself
from the pain.

2415
01:33:26,767 --> 01:33:27,967
You know, like,

2416
01:33:27,967 --> 01:33:29,600
yeah, the writer
was only interested

2417
01:33:29,600 --> 01:33:32,667
in shallow stereotypes
of mid-'60s sociopaths.

2418
01:33:32,667 --> 01:33:34,033
You just gotta deal with it.

2419
01:33:34,033 --> 01:33:35,400
- Oh, I see.

2420
01:33:35,400 --> 01:33:37,700
The villains were so
cliched, they were laughable!

2421
01:33:37,700 --> 01:33:38,633
(laughs)

2422
01:33:38,633 --> 01:33:40,567
- Right! That's it exactly.

2423
01:33:40,567 --> 01:33:41,900
- And the hero was such a wimp,

2424
01:33:41,900 --> 01:33:44,200
his only heroic act was
to flash his headlights.

2425
01:33:44,200 --> 01:33:45,200
That's funny!

2426
01:33:45,200 --> 01:33:46,167
(laughs)

2427
01:33:46,167 --> 01:33:47,600
- Yeah, you guys.

2428
01:33:47,600 --> 01:33:49,133
Keep in mind this is
during the Otto Preminger

2429
01:33:49,967 --> 01:33:50,900
time of film.

2430
01:33:50,900 --> 01:33:53,400
You know, like anti-hero,

2431
01:33:53,400 --> 01:33:54,800
plots that didn't go anywhere,

2432
01:33:54,800 --> 01:33:56,333
that kinda thing.

2433
01:33:56,333 --> 01:33:59,000
- So the hero was supposed to
be unattractive and spineless.

2434
01:33:59,000 --> 01:34:00,633
- Exactly! Now you're
surfing on my wave.

2435
01:34:00,633 --> 01:34:01,833
Take it, Tom Servo.

2436
01:34:01,833 --> 01:34:03,067
- Oh, um, well,

2437
01:34:03,067 --> 01:34:04,500
even though this was
one of the ugliest

2438
01:34:04,500 --> 01:34:06,533
extended families
in movie history,

2439
01:34:06,533 --> 01:34:09,467
they drove one of the finest
station wagons on the market!

2440
01:34:09,467 --> 01:34:12,167
- Hey! That was hysterical!

2441
01:34:12,167 --> 01:34:13,667
- You know, you're right, Joel.

2442
01:34:13,667 --> 01:34:16,400
Looking at the movie your
way makes me feel great!

2443
01:34:16,400 --> 01:34:19,100
- Yeah, I really like
this wild rebel thing!

2444
01:34:19,100 --> 01:34:20,367
Yahoo!

2445
01:34:20,367 --> 01:34:22,600
- What the hell is
going on up there?

2446
01:34:22,600 --> 01:34:24,467
- Really, I thought this
film was supposed to be

2447
01:34:24,467 --> 01:34:26,667
an emotional kneecapping
for you guys.

2448
01:34:26,667 --> 01:34:30,533
(dance music)
(Crow cheering)

2449
01:34:30,533 --> 01:34:33,167
- I don't believe it, Frank!

2450
01:34:33,167 --> 01:34:35,933
This film had absolutely
nothing going for it!

2451
01:34:35,933 --> 01:34:38,233
- An ugly cast
and an ugly script

2452
01:34:38,233 --> 01:34:41,567
doing really stupid, uh...

2453
01:34:41,567 --> 01:34:42,833
(chuckles)

2454
01:34:42,833 --> 01:34:44,067
I mean, wait a minute,
think about it though.

2455
01:34:44,067 --> 01:34:46,200
The Citrusville National Bank.

2456
01:34:46,200 --> 01:34:48,500
The hypodermic needle
putting the guard out.

2457
01:34:48,500 --> 01:34:51,033
I mean it was so stupid,
it was kind of funny.

2458
01:34:51,033 --> 01:34:52,600
It had wit, it had charm,

2459
01:34:52,600 --> 01:34:54,767
it was quirky, it was offbeat.

2460
01:34:54,767 --> 01:34:57,467
I'm gonna give this one my
highest rating: five skulls.

2461
01:34:57,467 --> 01:34:58,933
Woo!

2462
01:34:58,933 --> 01:35:01,267
- I really thought we
had you this time, Joely.

2463
01:35:01,267 --> 01:35:03,567
Don't you have a letter
to read or something?

2464
01:35:03,567 --> 01:35:06,900
(dance music, cheering)

2465
01:35:10,300 --> 01:35:11,733
- All right, all right, okay.

2466
01:35:11,733 --> 01:35:12,967
Back it off, you guys!

2467
01:35:12,967 --> 01:35:15,100
Cut it out, cut the
music, all right.

2468
01:35:15,100 --> 01:35:17,633
All right, we gotta
read a letter, you guys.

2469
01:35:17,633 --> 01:35:19,100
- [Servo] Oh, letters! Great!

2470
01:35:19,100 --> 01:35:20,967
- Yeah, this is an
interesting one.

2471
01:35:20,967 --> 01:35:24,400
It says, "Dear Joel, I
am in fact a scientist."

2472
01:35:24,400 --> 01:35:25,233
(balloon pops)

2473
01:35:25,233 --> 01:35:26,167
Excuse me.

2474
01:35:26,167 --> 01:35:27,800
"I am a PhD immunologist.

2475
01:35:27,800 --> 01:35:30,233
"I work a the Pittsburgh
Cancer Institute

2476
01:35:30,233 --> 01:35:32,067
"and study natural killer cells.

2477
01:35:32,067 --> 01:35:33,300
"What a great term that would be

2478
01:35:33,300 --> 01:35:35,333
"in a science fiction
movie," she writes.

2479
01:35:35,333 --> 01:35:38,067
"Perhaps my background gives
me a particular framework,

2480
01:35:38,067 --> 01:35:41,533
"but I am a devoted
MST 3000 fan.

2481
01:35:41,533 --> 01:35:43,667
"The letters you read each
week are still from children.

2482
01:35:43,667 --> 01:35:46,067
"I guess a letter from
a 30-year-old scientist

2483
01:35:46,067 --> 01:35:47,867
"without any drawings
doesn't have a prayer

2484
01:35:47,867 --> 01:35:49,067
"in making it on the air,

2485
01:35:49,067 --> 01:35:52,667
"so perhaps I should
come up with a drawing."

2486
01:35:52,667 --> 01:35:55,967
That's from Rebecca
P. Schell, PhD.

2487
01:35:55,967 --> 01:35:58,000
And here's the
drawing right there.

2488
01:35:58,000 --> 01:35:59,800
Let's get that on still
store there, Cambot.

2489
01:35:59,800 --> 01:36:01,300
- [Servo] Not bad for
a 30-year-old, huh?

2490
01:36:01,300 --> 01:36:02,567
- It says "Who will win?"

2491
01:36:02,567 --> 01:36:04,700
The Natural Killer
Cell or Tom Servo?

2492
01:36:04,700 --> 01:36:07,233
Hey, give us some more
music there, Cambot!

2493
01:36:07,233 --> 01:36:09,367
(dance music, cheering)

2494
01:36:09,367 --> 01:36:11,200
Okay, we'll see you later!

2495
01:36:11,200 --> 01:36:12,767
We're having a great time!

2496
01:36:12,767 --> 01:36:15,100
Wish you were here, scientists!

2497
01:36:15,100 --> 01:36:17,600
- No no no no,
you win this time.

2498
01:36:17,600 --> 01:36:18,900
As for me,

2499
01:36:18,900 --> 01:36:21,700
I've gotta put Frank
down for the night.

2500
01:36:21,700 --> 01:36:22,633
Until next time.

2501
01:36:23,733 --> 01:36:26,367
(Frank yells)

2502
01:36:26,367 --> 01:36:31,367
("The Love Theme from Mystery
Science Theater 3000")
